msgid "**Directory sign-in:** With ``svc-db-openldap`` deployed, ``configuration.yaml`` lists a ``command_line`` auth provider named ``LDAP`` after the built-in ``homeassistant`` provider, which keeps the owner and the MCP account. The provider runs ``files/python/ldap_login.py``: it searches the login name in the users OU, binds as that entry with the typed password and reads ``memberOf``. Members of ``cn=web-app-homeassistant-administrator`` get ``system-admin``, members of ``cn=web-app-homeassistant-user`` get ``system-users``, everyone else and every directory error is refused."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Directory sign-in:** With `svc-db-openldap` deployed, `configuration.yaml` lists a `command_line` auth provider named `LDAP` after the built-in `homeassistant` provider, which keeps the owner and the MCP account. The provider runs `files/python/ldap_login.py`: it searches the login name in the users OU, binds as that entry with the typed password and reads `memberOf`. Members of `cn=web-app-homeassistant-administrator` get `system-admin`, members of `cn=web-app-homeassistant-user` get `system-users`, everyone else and every directory error is refused."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Directory-owned accounts only.** The RBAC sync and the sign-in mapping demote or disable only accounts the directory owns: members of a role group and accounts linked to the Keycloak social login or the LDAP source. Service, API, website and customer accounts that a consumer created keep their roles and stay enabled. On a directory-owned account the sync revokes only the roles the mapping manages and never disables an account that still holds a role granted outside the mapping (such as `Security Check Approver` or `Security Check Editor`)."
