# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Docker Swarm as a second deployment mode.** Roles can now be deployed across multiple hosts instead of being limited to a single Compose stack. New *svc-swarm-node* initializes the cluster, while *svc-swarm-manager* marks the Raft managers in the inventory. Shared state is provided through *svc-storage-nfs-server* and *svc-storage-nfs-client*. *svc-registry-docker* distributes locally built images, and *svc-registry-cache* provides a Docker Hub pull-through cache so additional nodes do not multiply external pulls and rate-limit usage. Deployment, dependency resolution, networking, health checks and role templates now understand both Compose and Swarm semantics. See the [svc-swarm-node](roles/svc-swarm-node/README.md) and [svc-storage-nfs-server](roles/svc-storage-nfs-server/README.md) READMEs."
msgstr "**Docker Swarm som en anden implementering tilstand.** Roller kan nu anvendes på tværs af flere værter i stedet for at være begrænset til en enkelt komposition stak. Ny *svc-swarm-node* initialiserer klyngen, mens *svc-swarm-manager* markerer Raft-lederne i oversigten. Delstaten leveres gennem *svc-storage-nfs-server* og *svc-storage-nfs-client*. *svc-registry-docker* distribuerer lokalt byggede billeder, og *svc-registry-cache* giver en Docker Hub pullthrough cache, så yderligere knudepunkter ikke formere eksterne træk og rate- grænse brug. Implementering, afhængighedsopløsning, netværk, sundhedstjek og rolleskabeloner forstår nu både komposition og sværm semantik. Se [svc-swarm-node](roles/svc-swarm-node/README.md) og [svc-storage-nfs-server](roles/svc-storage-nfs-server/README.md) READMES."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Docker Swarm deployment mode** for any role whose own Ansible group lists more than one host. The cluster is bootstrapped by the `svc-swarm-node` group; per-role topology is derived from `groups[application_id]` directly. A role with one or zero hosts in its group stays on the existing Compose path and renders byte-identical output (no implicit migration). Adding additional hosts to a role's own group is the single trigger that promotes the role to a Swarm service."
msgstr "**Docker Swarm deployeringstilstand** for en hvilken som helst rolle, hvis egen Anible-gruppe anfører mere end én vært. klyngen er bootstrapped af `svc-swarm-node` gruppe; perrolletopologi er afledt af `groups[application_id]` direkte. En rolle med en eller nul værter i sin gruppe forbliver på den eksisterende Sammensæt sti og gør byte- identisk output (ingen implicit migration). Tilføjelse af yderligere værter til en rolles egen gruppe er den eneste udløser, der fremmer rollen til en Swarm service."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Docker Swarm secrets.** v1 keeps the existing env-file-based credential rendering (no app-side code changes). Migrating to `docker secret` (Raft-encrypted, mounted under `/run/secrets/<name>`) is a follow-up requirement and requires per-role app-code adaptations to read secrets from files instead of env vars."
msgstr "**Docker Swarm hemmeligheder.** v1 holder den eksisterende envfilbaserede credential rendering (ingen app- side kode ændringer). Migrerende til `docker secret` (Raft- krypteret, monteret under `/run/secrets/<name>`) er en opfølgning krav og kræver perrolle app- kode tilpasninger til at læse hemmeligheder fra filer i stedet for env vars."

