msgid "**Keycloak owns the Zammad roles:** every OIDC sign-in rewrites the account's roles from its RBAC group membership, as declared by `ZAMMAD_RBAC_ROLE_GRANTS` in [vars/main.yml](./vars/main.yml): `administrator` grants `Admin` and `Agent`, `agent` grants `Agent`, `customer` grants `Customer`, and a sign-in whose groups match none of them grants `Customer`. A role handed out by hand in the Zammad admin panel is therefore replaced at the account's next sign-in. The roles are left untouched, with an error in the Rails log, whenever the mapping cannot be applied: no group claim in the response at all, a granted role that Zammad does not have or has deactivated, or a role write Zammad's own guards refuse (the last admin, the agent limit). The native `Admin` + `Agent` account of [files/ruby/apply/administrator.rb](./files/ruby/apply/administrator.rb) is only converged while `sso` is off, and the OIDC path grants roles only, not the `Users` group access that script also sets."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Keycloak owns the Zammad roles:** every OIDC sign-in rewrites the account’s roles from its RBAC group membership, as declared by ``ZAMMAD_RBAC_ROLE_GRANTS`` in `vars/main.yml <./vars/main.yml>`__: ``administrator`` grants ``Admin`` and ``Agent``, ``agent`` grants ``Agent``, ``customer`` grants ``Customer``, and a sign-in whose groups match none of them grants ``Customer``. A role handed out by hand in the Zammad admin panel is therefore replaced at the account’s next sign-in. The roles are left untouched, with an error in the Rails log, whenever the mapping cannot be applied: no group claim in the response at all, a granted role that Zammad does not have or has deactivated, or a role write Zammad’s own guards refuse (the last admin, the agent limit). The native ``Admin`` + ``Agent`` account of `files/ruby/apply/administrator.rb <./files/ruby/apply/administrator.rb>`__ is only converged while ``sso`` is off, and the OIDC path grants roles only, not the ``Users`` group access that script also sets."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Keycloak sign-in:** With Keycloak in the deployment, the role sets ``services.sso.flavor: oidc`` and the LiteLLM Gateway reads the platform’s OIDC endpoints from ``GENERIC_CLIENT_ID``, ``GENERIC_CLIENT_SECRET``, ``GENERIC_AUTHORIZATION_ENDPOINT``, ``GENERIC_TOKEN_ENDPOINT`` and ``GENERIC_USERINFO_ENDPOINT``. Sign in at ``/sso/key/generate``; ``PROXY_ADMIN_ID`` carries the administrator’s username. LiteLLM serves SSO for up to five accounts in ``litellm_usertable`` and refuses beyond that without ``LITELLM_LICENSE``."
msgstr "**Keycloak sign- in:** Med Keycloak i indsættelsen, rollesæt ``services.sso.flavor: oidc`` og LiteLLM Gateway læser platformens OIDC endepunkter fra ``GENERIC_CLIENT_ID``, ``GENERIC_CLIENT_SECRET``, ``GENERIC_AUTHORIZATION_ENDPOINT``, ``GENERIC_TOKEN_ENDPOINT`` og ``GENERIC_USERINFO_ENDPOINT``. Log ind på ``/sso/key/generate``; ``PROXY_ADMIN_ID`` har administratorens brugernavn. LiteLLM betjener SSO for op til fem konti i ``litellm_usertable`` og nægter uden ``LITELLM_LICENSE``."

