# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Search allocation precheck:** [search_allocation_precheck.sh](files/shell/search_allocation_precheck.sh) creates a one-shard probe index named after the container and fails with the answer of `_cluster/allocation/explain`, which names the disk watermark when the data disk is too full, unless Elasticsearch allocates it. `init` runs it in front of `zammad-init`. In compose, the one-shot `precheck` service runs it first and `init` depends on that service, so `compose up` stops on a refusal. Swarm renders no `precheck` service, because `depends_on` does not gate `init` there. Instead the deploy waits until the newest `init` task is `Complete`: a refusing Elasticsearch leaves it `Failed`, the wait stops the deploy, and `docker service logs` of `init` carries the explanation. An `init` the stack deploy did not restart is already `Complete` and passes at once."
msgstr "**Forhåndscheck af søgetildeling:** [search_allocation_precheck.sh](files/shell/search_allocation_precheck.sh) skaber en one-shard sonde indeks opkaldt efter beholderen og mislykkes med svaret på `_cluster/allocation/explain`, som navngiver disk vandmærke, når data disk er for fuld, medmindre Elasticsearch allokerer det. `init` kører det foran `zammad-init`. I komponere, den one-shot `precheck` service kører det først og `init` afhænger af denne service, så `compose up` stopper med at nægte. Sværm giver ingen `precheck` service, fordi `depends_on` låser ikke `init` Der. I stedet for venter deployeringen indtil den nyeste `init` opgave er `Complete`: et afslag Elasticsearch efterlader det `Failed`, ventetiden stopper deployeringen, og `docker service logs` af `init` bærer forklaringen. En `init` stakken deployering ikke genstarte er allerede `Complete` og passerer på én gang."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Search allocation precheck:** `search_allocation_precheck.sh <files/shell/search_allocation_precheck.sh>`__ creates a one-shard probe index named after the container and fails with the answer of ``_cluster/allocation/explain``, which names the disk watermark when the data disk is too full, unless Elasticsearch allocates it. ``init`` runs it in front of ``zammad-init``. In compose, the one-shot ``precheck`` service runs it first and ``init`` depends on that service, so ``compose up`` stops on a refusal. Swarm renders no ``precheck`` service, because ``depends_on`` does not gate ``init`` there. Instead the deploy waits until the newest ``init`` task is ``Complete``: a refusing Elasticsearch leaves it ``Failed``, the wait stops the deploy, and ``docker service logs`` of ``init`` carries the explanation. An ``init`` the stack deploy did not restart is already ``Complete`` and passes at once."
msgstr "**Forhåndscheck af søgetildeling:** `search_allocation_precheck.sh <files/shell/search_allocation_precheck.sh>`__ skaber en one-shard sonde indeks opkaldt efter beholderen og mislykkes med svaret på ``_cluster/allocation/explain``, som navngiver disk vandmærke, når data disk er for fuld, medmindre Elasticsearch allokerer det. ``init`` kører det foran ``zammad-init``. I komponere, den one-shot ``precheck`` service kører det først og ``init`` afhænger af denne service, så ``compose up`` stopper med at nægte. Sværm giver ingen ``precheck`` service, fordi ``depends_on`` låser ikke ``init`` Der. I stedet for venter deployeringen indtil den nyeste ``init`` opgave er ``Complete``: et afslag Elasticsearch efterlader det ``Failed``, ventetiden stopper deployeringen, og ``docker service logs`` af ``init`` bærer forklaringen. En ``init`` stakken deployering ikke genstarte er allerede ``Complete`` og passerer på én gang."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Search index per Elasticsearch major:** The index lives in a directory named after the Elasticsearch major inside the ``zammad_search`` volume. A new major starts on an empty directory and ``zammad-init`` rebuilds the index from the database on the same deploy."
msgstr "**Søgeindeks pr. Elasticsearch større:** Indekset bor i en mappe opkaldt efter Elasticsearch store inde i ``zammad_search`` volumen. En ny større starter på en tom mappe og ``zammad-init`` genopbygger indekset fra databasen på samme implementering."

