msgstr "En procentdel er den eneste bærbare måde at størrelse mod maskinen. Docker nægter en `cpus` over værtens kerne tæller (`range of CPUs is from 0.01 to N.00`), så `cpus: \"4\"` er en hård fiasko på en tokernet vært, mens `50%` er gyldigt overalt. `100%` Jeg vil gerne sige, at jeg er enig med ordføreren i, at det er vigtigt, at vi gør det."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A persona scenario MUST fail loudly when its contracted journey cannot execute end-to-end. A silent `test.skip(...)` on runtime detection of \"no logout button\", \"no authenticated surface\", or \"no admin UI marker\" is FORBIDDEN. Silent skips hide real regressions (broken OIDC mapping, removed logout button, misconfigured oauth2-proxy, drifted UI selectors) behind a green deploy."
msgstr "En persona scenario SKAL mislykkes højt, når den aftalte rejse ikke kan udføre end-to-end. En tavs `test.skip(...)` ved påvisning af \"ingen logout- knap\", \"ingen godkendt overflade\"eller \"ingen admin UI markør\" sa FORBIDEN. Silent spring skjule rigtige regressioner (brudt OIDC mapping, fjernet logout knap, forkert konfigureret oauth2-proxy, drev UI selectors) bag en grøn deployering."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A persona scenario that only logs in and logs out is NOT enough. After the auth chain settles (or directly on the role surface when no auth is required), every persona MUST drive a real, app-specific interaction so the spec proves the role is responsive to user input, not just reachable."
msgstr "En persona scenario, der kun logger ind og logger ud er IKKE nok. Efter auth kæde bosætter sig (eller direkte på rolleoverfladen, når der ikke kræves godkendelse), hver persona SKAL køre en reel, app- specifik interaktion, så spec viser, at rollen er lydhør over for brugerinput, ikke bare tilgængelig."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A personal digital sovereignty stack for individuals controlling their own data."
msgstr "En personlig digital suverænitet stak for enkeltpersoner, der kontrollerer deres egne data."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A pin MUST be a quoted string, never an unquoted number. `\"\"` tracks the app default."
msgstr "En nål SKAL være en citeret streng, aldrig et uciteret tal. `\"\"` sporer appen standard."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A pin cannot be resolved."
msgstr "En nål kan ikke løses."

msgid "A pin is in force only while the role carrying it is part of the round's include and runs the variant the marker stands in. A pin in a role the round does not deploy changes nothing. The round starts every role on its clamped index and recomputes the include and the pins in force until the assignment no longer changes; pins that never settle raise `VariantPinError`. [test_variant_pin_fixed_point.py](../../../../../tests/integration/roles/meta/variants/test_variant_pin_fixed_point.py) settles every round the matrix plans (each role as the only primary, in each of its variants) and fails when a round raises `VariantPinError`, or when a pin in force stands above a service entry the carrier runs with `enabled: false` in that round. Place a pin only above an entry the variant keeps enabled: the guide host `docs` stays on for the primary app alone, so a pin above `docs` fails the guard in any round that pulls the role in as a dependency running that variant."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A pin lives either in the block of its entity in ``meta/services.yml`` or at the root of a ``meta/addons/<id>.yml``. The updater has to find its line to rewrite exactly that one, so the search is textual: parsing and re-emitting the YAML would reformat every other line of the file."
msgstr "En pin lever enten i blokken af sin enhed i ``meta/services.yml`` eller ved roden af en ``meta/addons/<id>.yml``. Den updater nødt til at finde sin linje til at omskrive præcis den ene, så søgningen er tekstmæssig: fortolkning og re- emittering af YAML ville omformatere hver anden linje i filen."

msgid "A pin of a role outside the include does not count, and neither does a pin above an entry the carrier runs switched off:"
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A pin states the dependency instead of inheriting it. Written as a comment on the line above the service entry that creates the dependency, it keeps the runtime services map clean: the marker never reaches ``host_vars``, unlike a YAML key under the service would::"
msgstr "En nål angiver afhængigheden i stedet for at arve den. Skrevet som en kommentar til den linje over tjenesten, der skaber afhængighed, det holder runtime tjenester kort: markøren aldrig når ``host_vars``, i modsætning til en YAML nøgle under tjenesten ville:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A pin the Docker updater (`image` + `version`) and the repository updater (`repository` + `ref`) do not reach names its upstream next to itself:"
msgstr "En nål Docker updater (`image` + `version`) og datalageret (`repository` + `ref`) ikke nå navne sin opstrøms ved siden af sig selv:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A platform may refuse a window it considers too small. Hermes requires 64000 tokens and answers `HTTP 500` with \"below the minimum 64,000 required by Hermes Agent\" for anything less, so `web-app-hermes` declares `services.hermes.min_context` and the broker withholds any platform whose minimum the selected model misses: it is absent from `/v1/models` and answers 404, while every other platform keeps serving. Refusing the whole deploy instead would block a pairing that works, since OpenClaw declares no minimum and the broker pulls Hermes into its closure either way. A model that declares no window at all is reported rather than withheld: an agent that does not know its window runs."
msgstr "En platform kan afvise et vindue, den anser for for lille. Hermes kræver 64000 tokens og svar `HTTP 500` med \"under minimum 64,000 kræves af Hermes Agent\" for noget mindre, så `web-app-hermes` erklærer `services.hermes.min_context` og mægleren tilbageholder enhver platform, hvis minimum den valgte model savner: det er fraværende fra `/v1/models` og svar 404, mens alle andre platforme bliver ved med at tjene. At afvise hele deployeringen i stedet ville blokere en parring, der virker, da OpenClaw erklærer ingen minimum og mægleren trækker Hermes ind i sin lukning enten måde. En model, der erklærer intet vindue overhovedet er rapporteret snarere end tilbageholdt: en agent, der ikke kender dens vindue kører."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A plug-and-go backup of the local backup tree to an external block device (typically a swappable USB drive). The transfer is hard-link deduplicated against the previous snapshot, so each plug-in yields a complete, browsable point-in-time copy without doubling disk usage."
msgstr "En plug- and- go backup af det lokale backup træ til en ekstern blok enhed (typisk en swappbar USB-drev). Overførslen er hard- link deduplikeret mod det forrige øjebliksbillede, så hver plug-in giver en komplet, browserbar point- in- time kopi uden fordobling disk brug."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A plugin MAY ship an appstore release that lags the pinned Nextcloud server major. In that case OCC emits the marker string `is not compatible with this version of the server` and exits non-zero. The pipeline MUST treat this as a non-fatal condition:"
msgstr "Et plugin MAJ sende en appstore udgivelse, der halter den fæstede Nextcloud server major. I så fald udsender OCC markørstrengen `is not compatible with this version of the server` og forlader non-nul. Rørledningen SKAL behandle dette som en ikke-dødelig tilstand:"

msgid "A plugin entry MAY set `mandatory: true`. This inverts the tolerance above: when the plugin is `enabled` for the current deployment but its install result is not `runnable` (incompatible with the pinned server major, or unavailable on the appstore), [02_install.yml](./02_install.yml) aborts the deployment with `ansible.builtin.fail` instead of emitting the skip warning."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A pool of two or more stays a preference because the matrix already narrowed each row to one kind out of it: falling back to the other kind the run allowed is inside what the operator asked for, while failing the row is not. A run whose whole pool is unservable fails rather than leaving the pool."
msgstr "En pulje af to eller flere forbliver en præference, fordi matrixen allerede indsnævret hver række til en slags ud af det: falder tilbage til den anden slags løbeturen tilladt er inde i, hvad operatøren bad om, mens manglende rækken er ikke. En løbetur, hvis hele pool ikke kan betjenes, slår fejl i stedet for at forlade poolen."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A pool or token of exactly one kind is read as a human naming it, so the applying step **fails the row instead of substituting** a kind the host can serve. Pinning a kind the runner cannot deliver therefore produces a red job that says nothing about the question."
msgstr "En pulje eller et symbol af præcis én slags læses som et menneske navngivning det, så det anvendte trin **mislykkes rækken i stedet for at erstatte** en slags værten kan tjene. At blande en slags løber kan derfor ikke levere et rødt job, der ikke siger noget om spørgsmålet."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A practical long-term target is:"
msgstr "Et praktisk langsigtet mål er:"

msgid "A pre-flight check probes a host before a deploy changes it and stops the deploy when the host is in a state the deploy cannot recover from on its own: a kernel without its modules, a full disk, a docker object that belongs to another project, a port a host service already holds, or a domain that does not resolve."
msgstr ""

# holder dommen og præfikset kun en timing -- den komponerede startperiode er
# den længste af de to, aldrig præfikset er alene. At sænke det en gang ville
# have skåret et 15 minutters start vindue ned til to.
# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A prefix cannot judge the container, so the probe keeps the verdict and the prefix only ever RAISES a timing -- the composed start period is the longest of the two, never the prefix's alone. Lowering it once would have cut a fifteen minute start window down to two."
msgstr "Et præfiks kan ikke bedømme beholderen, så sonden holder dommen og præfikset kun en timing -- den komponerede startperiode er den længste af de to, aldrig præfikset er alene. At sænke det en gang ville have skåret et 15 minutters start vindue ned til to."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A prefix does something on the way past -- sending a smoke mail is the only one so far -- and deliberately cannot decide liveness. That separation is what lets a probe stay the single verdict."
msgstr "Et præfiks gør noget på vejen forbi -- at sende en røgpost er den eneste indtil videre -- og kan bevidst ikke beslutte løgnagtighed. Den adskillelse lader en sonde forblive den eneste dom."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A prefix mask leaves a contiguous run of low bits free, so per octet the addresses span exactly ``network_address`` to ``broadcast_address``. The cross product of those four ranges is the network, which makes the octet decomposition exact for any prefix length, aligned or not."
msgstr "En præfiks maske efterlader et sammenhængende løb af lave bits gratis, så pr octet adresserne span præcis ``network_address`` til ``broadcast_address``. Krydsproduktet af disse fire intervaller er netværket, som gør octet nedbrydning eksakt for enhver præfiks længde, justeret eller ej."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A priority entry may pin axes (``web-app-zammad#1@compose+tor``), and the pin rides along into the retrigger: the entry never ran, so the run holds no evidence that the axes it named were the wrong ones. Only the name in front of the axis suffix is resolved against the statuses."
msgstr "En prioriteret indgang kan fastgøre akser (``web-app-zammad#1@compose+tor``), og stiften rider langs ind i genudløser: indgangen aldrig løb, så løbeturen indeholder intet bevis for, at økserne det navngivne var de forkerte. Kun navnet foran aksens suffiks løses mod statusserne."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A priority role can fall behind the discovery budget cut in every mode, so the run holds no job for it and :func:`failed_roles` cannot see it — it is neither green nor red, it simply never ran. Carrying it into the retrigger is the only way it ever gets deployed."
msgstr "En prioriteret rolle kan falde bag den opdagelse budget nedskæringer i hver mode, så løb ikke har noget job for det og :func:`failed_roles` kan ikke se det - det er hverken grønt eller rødt, det simpelthen aldrig løb. At bære den ind i udløseren er den eneste måde, den bliver indsat på."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A privacy-first foundation for enterprises running AI locally and keeping sensitive data on-prem."
msgstr "En privat-første fond for virksomheder, der kører AI lokalt og holde følsomme data on-prem."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A process stuck in `D` cannot be killed and is the host-visible trace of a wedged mount. Only the state field is evaluated; the command name is never retained, so the count can be logged without leaking process command lines. The comm field may itself contain spaces and `)`, so the state is read after the last closing parenthesis rather than by index."
msgstr "En proces fast i `D` kan ikke dræbes og er den vært- synlige spor af en kilet mount. Kun statsfeltet evalueres; kommandonavnet bevares aldrig, så tællingen kan logges uden at lække kommandolinjer. Kommunikationsfeltet kan selv indeholde mellemrum og `)`, så staten er læst efter den sidste lukning parentes snarere end ved indeks."

msgid "A process that renders network-bound URLs once (one callback, one config) serves a single network, so an application served on several networks runs one such process per network."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A professional collaboration and identity management stack for modern organizations."
msgstr "Et professionelt samarbejde og identitetsstyringsstack for moderne organisationer."

msgid "A profile change made in Keycloak reaches Nextcloud on the next run of `files/python/ldap_refresh.py` (deploy or RBAC timer), a native LDAP login or the `user_ldap` background sync, not at the OIDC login itself: `oidc_login` in LDAP proxy mode fetches the DN without attributes (read from `LoginService::getLDAPUserUid` and `Access::fetchListOfUsers`), and no Playwright scenario can wait for a timer run. Options: an upstream `oidc_login` change that refreshes the LDAP record at login."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A prompt above the server's state limit is truncated rather than rejected as a routing failure"
msgstr "En prompt over serverens statsgrænse er afkortet snarere end afvist som en routing fiasko"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A prose deprecation value is not read as a date"
msgstr "En prosedetermineringsværdi læses ikke som en dato"

msgid "A provider declares ``overlay.stream_relay`` with a ``switch`` and the ``ports`` it opens. While the switch is true and the reverse proxy's own overlay applies in the mode, the provider and the reverse proxy share ``<entity>-relay`` and nothing else does, so the relay never puts the proxy on the provider's overlay with its consumers."
msgstr ""

msgid "A provider declares `overlay.stream_relay` in its `meta/networks.yml` with a `switch` (a config path on the provider), the `ports` it relays and the `subnet` of the relay network. While the switch is true, and only in the modes where the reverse proxy (`svc-prx-openresty`) itself runs on overlays (its own `networks.overlay.modes`, today `[swarm]`), the provider and the reverse proxy join a dedicated network `<entity>-relay` (`openldap-relay`), and no other role joins it. The provider carries its entity name as alias there. The reverse proxy never joins the provider's overlay. In compose openresty keeps the host network and reaches the published loopback port as before."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A provider writes its credential to the token store during its own role run, and each client resolves the providers it may reach from that store. This role runs at the end of the server stage, after every provider has written and before the end-to-end tests read the converged state."
msgstr "En udbyder skriver sin kreditværdighed til token butik under sin egen rolle køre, og hver klient løser de udbydere, det kan nå fra denne butik. Denne rolle kører i slutningen af serveren fase, efter at hver udbyder har skrevet og før end-to-end test læse den konvergerede tilstand."

msgid "A proving line carries the marker and a run token (``✓``/passed) and is not a skip line; a line that only skips the marker (a leading ``-`` or the word ``skipped``) does not count, so a guarded spec reported as skipped is not mistaken for executed."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A proxy repo that holds a cached copy serves it when its remote is unreachable, regardless of `metadataMaxAge` (measured). `autoBlock` is therefore off: while a remote is auto-blocked Nexus answers `404 Remote Auto Blocked` instead of falling back to that cached copy. The mirror repos below only come into play when nothing is cached either."
msgstr "En proxy repo, der holder en cache kopi tjener det, når dens fjernbetjening er utilgængelig, uanset om `metadataMaxAge` (målt). `autoBlock` er derfor slukket: mens en fjernbetjening er auto-blokeret Nexus svar `404 Remote Auto Blocked` I stedet for at falde tilbage til denne cached kopi. Spejlet repos nedenfor kommer kun i spil, når intet er cachet enten."

msgid "A pull request labelled as touching protected paths is never recommended for merge; the review names the touched paths and leaves the decision to a human."
msgstr ""

msgid "A pull stages every declared role in a work directory outside ``roles/`` and checks it before the first entry of ``roles/`` changes, so a refused pull leaves ``roles/`` as it was. A pull or clean only ever replaces or removes the directories the pull placed itself, whose marker names them."
msgstr ""

msgid "A pull stages every role outside `roles/` and changes `roles/` only when all of them passed, so a refused pull leaves it as it was. It replaces or removes only the directories it placed itself, whose marker names them, and refuses a declared name that meets a symbolic link, a hand-placed directory or a copy of a placed role. `make roles-clean` removes every `roles/web-app-cst-*` directory the pull placed and reports every other one it leaves in place. Git ignores `roles/web-app-cst-*`, so a pulled role never enters a core commit."
msgstr ""

msgid "A pull stops while any of these files cannot be read: a declaration it cannot see would make it remove the role as no longer declared."
msgstr ""

msgid "A quality gate outranks both crons: while the machine's gate lock is held, the translator stays paused, at night as well, and resumes when the lock is released."
msgstr ""

msgid "A quality gate outranks every long-running job on the same machine (translation, deploys, builds, other gates): before the gate starts, the gate routine takes the machine's gate lock and pauses every running long job (the translation lane through `make i18n-pause`); after the gate ends, it releases the lock and resumes them. No agent writes to the tree under test while the gate runs. A gate that ran with a long job beside it is discarded, not judged."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A question MUST NOT modify files, code, or state. Only explicit commands MAY."
msgstr "Et spørgsmål SKAL IKKE ændre filer, kode eller tilstand. Kun eksplicitte kommandoer MAJ."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A random bearer key per agent, known only to the broker, used in both directions."
msgstr "En tilfældig bærer nøgle per agent, kun kendt af mægleren, anvendes i begge retninger."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A rapid deployment stack for startups building software products and services."
msgstr "En hurtig implementering stak til nystartede byggesoftware produkter og tjenester."

msgid "A re-entrant call returns before ``_MERGED_APPLICATIONS_CACHE`` is written, because its payload carries no users and keeps its volumes. It is therefore memoised on the render guard instead, which drops it when the guard releases. Without that, one template render recomputed the payload for every ``lookup('applications')`` it made."
msgstr ""

msgid "A read without a templar (the raw users inside an applications render) never takes the carrier."
msgstr ""

msgid "A readable injected sheet lets LibreTranslate rewrite the shared sheet's `prefers-color-scheme` at load; keep the injected links without `crossorigin` and shield such apps in the role `design.js`."
msgstr ""

msgid "A real upstream or licence limit keeps the item open with its reason; no workaround."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A record MUST NOT be written for a choice that a reader can recover from the code alone, such as a helper's signature or a local refactoring."
msgstr "En record SKAL IKKE skrives for et valg, at en læser kan komme sig fra koden alene, såsom en hjælper underskrift eller en lokal refactoring."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A record MUST be numbered in the order it was accepted, and its number MUST NOT be reused."
msgstr "En plade skal nummereres i den rækkefølge, den blev godkendt, og dens nummer må ikke genbruges."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A record MUST cover a decision whose reversal would be expensive: a contract between components, a data or naming shape other code depends on, or a rule that governs a whole subsystem."
msgstr "En record SKAL dække en beslutning, hvis vending ville være dyr: en kontrakt mellem komponenter, en data eller navngivning anden kode afhænger af, eller en regel, der regulerer et helt delsystem."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A record MUST describe the decision as it stands today, including the alternatives that were weighed and why they lost, so a later reader can tell a deliberate constraint from an accident."
msgstr "En rekord SKAL beskrive beslutningen, som den er i dag, herunder de alternativer, der blev vejet og hvorfor de tabte, så en senere læser kan fortælle en bevidst begrænsning fra en ulykke."

msgid "A record newer than the image stops the deploy and leaves the volume untouched."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A recover mirrors a snapshot into a live target directory (``rsync -aHAX --delete``), so the target's current state would be lost without a net. The flow therefore first runs the role's deployed backup service (``systemctl start`` on the role's unit), which applies the usual differential backup logic to the live data before anything is overwritten. Roles subclass :class:`DirectoryRecovery`, set ``unit_pattern`` and ship a thin ``files/python/recover.py`` CLI around it (enforced by ``tests/lint/ansible/roles/test_bkp_roles_have_recover.py``)."
msgstr "En gendanne spejle et øjebliksbillede i en levende målmappe (``rsync -aHAX --delete``), Så målet ville gå tabt uden et net. Flowet derfor først kører rollens indsat backup service (``systemctl start`` om rollens enhed), som anvender den sædvanlige differentiale backup logik til de levende data, før noget er overskrevet. Underklasse ruller :class:`DirectoryRecovery`, set ``unit_pattern`` og sende en tynd ``files/python/recover.py`` CLI rundt om det (håndhæves af ``tests/lint/ansible/roles/test_bkp_roles_have_recover.py``)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A recurring property of these extensions is that many of them exist **only to bridge into another role**: `ldapauth` and `user_ldap` bridge to `svc-db-openldap`; `sociallogin`, `oidc-authenticator`, `OpenIDConnect`, `plg_system_keycloak`, and the WordPress OIDC plugin bridge to the SSO provider (`web-app-keycloak`); `wp-discourse` bridges to `web-app-discourse`; XWiki's `ai-llm` extension bridges to `web-app-litellm`. Today that bridge is implicit. This requirement makes it explicit: **an addon that bridges to another role MUST declare the bridged service, and that service MUST be present in the role's `meta/services.yml`.**"
msgstr "En tilbagevendende egenskab ved disse udvidelser er, at mange af dem findes **kun at bygge bro til en anden rolle**: `ldapauth` og `user_ldap` bro til `svc-db-openldap`; `sociallogin`, `oidc-authenticator`, `OpenIDConnect`, `plg_system_keycloak`, og WordPress OIDC plugin bro til SSO udbyder (`web-app-keycloak`); `wp-discourse` broer til `web-app-discourse`; XWikis `ai-llm` forlængelsesbroer til `web-app-litellm`. I dag er broen implicit. Dette krav gør det udtrykkeligt: **en addon, at broer til en anden rolle SKAL erklære den brolagte tjeneste, og at tjenesten SKAL være til stede i rollens `meta/services.yml`.**"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A red job could not be reproduced by re-running its sweep, which is the property the whole rotation exists to provide."
msgstr "Et rødt job kunne ikke reproduceres ved at køre sin sweep igen, hvilket er den egenskab, hele rotation findes at levere."

msgid "A redeploy of an unchanged version includes [`03_upgrade/02_cached_updates.yml`](./tasks/02_manager_ops/03_upgrade/02_cached_updates.yml) instead, which updates apps without querying the appstore:"
msgstr ""

msgid "A redeploy of an unchanged version includes ```03_upgrade/02_cached_updates.yml`` <./tasks/02_manager_ops/03_upgrade/02_cached_updates.yml>`__ instead, which updates apps without querying the appstore:"
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A refusal names the token and why. Fix the token, never the check: a variant that no longer exists means the list was carried over from an older run, and dropping the pin only moves the wrong row into the queue."
msgstr "Et afslag giver tegn og hvorfor. Fastsætte token, aldrig check: en variant, der ikke længere eksisterer betyder, at listen blev fremført fra en ældre køre, og droppe stiften kun flytter den forkerte række ind i køen."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A refusal records what the server answered under the masking of the day. A source change clears it by itself, because the entry is then new; a change to the masking or to the damage predicate does not, and those entries would stay skipped forever."
msgstr "En afvisning registrerer, hvad serveren svarede under maskering af dagen. En kildeændring rydder det af sig selv, fordi indgangen er så ny; en ændring til maskering eller til skaden forudsiger ikke, og disse poster ville forblive sprunget over for evigt."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A refused answer reaches the next engine"
msgstr "Et afvist svar når den næste motor"

# ``192\.168\.24\.\d+`` for a /24 eller ``192\.168\.(24|25)\.\d+`` for a /23.
# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A regex over dotted octets, e.g. ``192\\.168\\.24\\.\\d+`` for a /24 or ``192\\.168\\.(24|25)\\.\\d+`` for a /23."
msgstr "En regex over stiplede ottedele, f.eks. ``192\\.168\\.24\\.\\d+`` for a /24 eller ``192\\.168\\.(24|25)\\.\\d+`` for a /23."

msgid "A release tag (``vX.Y.Z``) is built the first time someone opens it. The browser shows a progress bar and reloads once the build is done. Tags never change, so a tag is built again only after the cap in point 6 dropped it."
msgstr ""

msgid "A release tag (`vX.Y.Z`) is built the first time someone opens it. The browser shows a progress bar and reloads once the build is done. Tags never change, so a tag is built again only after the cap in point 6 dropped it."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A remote source (``[user@]host:/path``) is returned as-is with the default target (its colon is the rsync host separator). Otherwise a colon suffix is a restore target only when absolute; a relative suffix is rejected here (device parses those itself)."
msgstr "En ekstern kilde (``[user@]host:/path``) returneres as- er med standardmålet (dens kolon er rsync vært separator)Ellers er et kolonsuffiks kun et genoprettelsesmål, når det er absolut; et relativt suffiks afvises her (enhed parser dem selv)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A rendered ``socialhome.toml`` is mounted alongside the environment file. It carries exactly one setting — ``[standalone].external_url`` — because that value has no ``SH_*`` environment equivalent upstream and federation pairing returns ``422 NOT_CONFIGURED`` without it."
