msgid "A role MAY omit the file entirely. The loader then exposes exactly one variant equal to the assembled per-role meta payload (`meta/services.yml` + `meta/server.yml` + `meta/rbac.yml` + `meta/volumes.yml` + `apply_schema()`'d `meta/secrets.yml`) unchanged."
msgstr "En rolle MAJ udelade filen helt. Den loader derefter udsætter præcis en variant svarende til den samlede perrolle meta nyttelast (`meta/services.yml` + `meta/server.yml` + `meta/rbac.yml` + `meta/volumes.yml` + `apply_schema()`' `meta/secrets.yml`) uændret."

# translated-by: libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "A role MAY ship `templates/design.js`, or `templates/design.js.j2` when it needs Jinja. `sys-front-inj-design` carries the per-app config `{logo, title, urls}` in the script tag's `data-design` attribute and prepends a line that reads it into `INFINITO_DESIGN`, collapses the result, adds its CSP hash and injects it whenever `services.design.enabled` is enabled, independent of `services.javascript.enabled`. The config rides in the attribute because CSP hashes only the script body: an onion vhost rewrites the CDN host in the payload, and a body holding that host would no longer match its hash. For the same reason a design script MUST read branding through `INFINITO_DESIGN` and MUST NOT interpolate `design.urls` itself."
msgstr "En rolle MAJ skib `templates/design.js`, eller `templates/design.js.j2` når den har brug for Jinja. `sys-front-inj-design` bærer per- app config `{logo, title, urls}` i script tags `data-design` attribut og udregner en linje, der læser det i `INFINITO_DESIGN`, kollapser resultatet, tilføjer sin CSP hash og injicerer det, når `services.design.enabled` er aktiveret, uafhængigt af `services.javascript.enabled`. Den config rides i attributten, fordi CSP hashes kun scriptet krop: et løg vhost omskriver CDN vært i nyttelasten, og en krop bedrift, at værten ikke længere ville matche sin hash. Af samme grund et design script SKAL læse branding gennem `INFINITO_DESIGN` og må ikke interpolere `design.urls` selv."

