# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A role keeps declaring the service for inventory completeness but can opt out of this consumer-target list by setting ``services.<service>.scrape: false`` or ``services.<service>.track: false``. ``scrape: false`` is used by 301-redirect-only vhosts that declare ``services.prometheus`` (so the role-wiring contract stays satisfied) yet never serve a request through lua-resty-prometheus, so they emit no ``app=\"<role>\"`` label and have no scrape target. ``track: false`` is the symmetric matomo opt-out: static-file (autoindex) and 301-redirect vhosts that declare ``services.matomo`` keep the role-wiring intact but carry no user-facing HTML page worth a ``_paq`` tracker, so they are dropped from ``MATOMO_TARGET_ROLES_JSON`` and the matomo tracker e2e contract."
msgstr "En rolle holder erklære tjenesten for opgørelse fuldstændighed, men kan fravælge denne forbruger-målliste ved at indstille ``services.<service>.scrape: false`` eller ``services.<service>.track: false``. ``scrape: false`` anvendes af 301-redirect- kun vhosts, der erklærer ``services.prometheus`` (så role- ledninger kontrakt forbliver tilfreds) men aldrig tjene en anmodning gennem lua-resty- prometheus, så de udsender ``app=\"<role>\"`` mærke og har ingen skrabe mål. ``track: false`` er den symmetriske matomo opt- out: statisk-fil (autoindeks) og 301-omdirigere vhosts, der erklærer ``services.matomo`` holde role- ledninger intakt, men bære ingen bruger- vender HTML-side værd en ``_paq`` Tracker, så de bliver droppet fra ``MATOMO_TARGET_ROLES_JSON`` og matomo tracker e2e kontrakt."

