# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A scheduled differential backup of the NFS export onto the local backup directory. Each run stores a discrete snapshot under `<backups>/<machine-hash>/backup-nfs-to-local/<generation>/files/`, hard-linked against the previous generation via rsync `--link-dest`."
msgstr "En planlagt differentieret backup af NFS eksport til den lokale backup mappe. Hvert løb gemmer et diskret snapshot under `<backups>/<machine-hash>/backup-nfs-to-local/<generation>/files/`, hard- linked mod den forrige generation via rsync `--link-dest`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A scheduled differential backup of the NFS export onto the local backup directory. Each run stores a discrete snapshot under ``<backups>/<machine-hash>/backup-nfs-to-local/<generation>/files/``, hard-linked against the previous generation via rsync ``--link-dest``."
msgstr "En planlagt differentieret backup af NFS eksport til den lokale backup mappe. Hvert løb gemmer et diskret snapshot under ``<backups>/<machine-hash>/backup-nfs-to-local/<generation>/files/``, hard- linked mod den forrige generation via rsync ``--link-dest``."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A scheduled pull-style backup that replicates the backup trees of one or more remote provider hosts onto this host via SSH + rsync. The receiving side is the trust anchor: each retrieval is a discrete snapshot, hard-linked against the previous one, with a retry loop guarding against transient network failures."
msgstr "En planlagt pull- stil backup, der kopierer backup træer af en eller flere fjernudbyder værter på denne vært via SSH + rsync. Den modtagende side er trust anker: hver hentning er en diskret snapshot, hard- forbundet med den foregående, med en prøve sløjfe bevogtning mod forbigående netværksfejl."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A scheduled workflow (`cron-*.yml`) drops the `Category:` schema: its `name:` MUST read as one short sentence saying what the run does, because the Actions list shows scheduled runs next to each other with no PR or branch to tell them apart."
msgstr "En planlagt arbejdsgang (`cron-*.yml`) falder `Category:` skema: dens `name:` SKAL læses som en kort sætning, der siger, hvad løbet gør, fordi listen Handlinger viser planlagte kører ved siden af hinanden uden nogen PR eller gren til at skelne dem fra hinanden."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A scheduled, deduplicating backup of every Docker container's data on this host to a local backup directory. File payloads are captured with rsync hard-link snapshots; databases register themselves into a central seed file so each backup run also dumps a consistent SQL snapshot via [baudolo](https://github.com/kevinveenbirkenbach/backup-docker-to-local)."
msgstr "En planlagt, duplikerende backup af hver Docker container data på denne vært til en lokal backup mappe. Filer nyttelaster er fanget med rsync hard- link snapshots; databaser registrere sig i en central seed-fil, så hver backup køre også dumper en konsekvent SQL snapshots via [baudolo](https://github.com/kevinveenbirkenbach/backup-docker-to-local)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A scheduled, deduplicating backup of every Docker container’s data on this host to a local backup directory. File payloads are captured with rsync hard-link snapshots; databases register themselves into a central seed file so each backup run also dumps a consistent SQL snapshot via `baudolo <https://github.com/kevinveenbirkenbach/backup-docker-to-local>`__."
msgstr "En planlagt, duplikerende backup af hver Docker container data på denne vært til en lokal backup mappe. Filer nyttelaster er fanget med rsync hard- link snapshots; databaser registrere sig i en central seed-fil, så hver backup køre også dumper en konsekvent SQL snapshots via `baudolo <https://github.com/kevinveenbirkenbach/backup-docker-to-local>`__."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A scheduled, deduplicating backup of the host's generated secret material to the local backup directory: the Infinito.Nexus secrets and tokens, the self-signed root CA, the Let's Encrypt account + certificates, the ACME DNS credentials, and the node identity (ssh host keys + machine-id). None of this lives in a docker volume, the NFS export or the operator inventory, so it is the gap the volume/nfs backup roles do not cover."
msgstr "En planlagt, duplikering backup af værtens genererede hemmelige materiale til den lokale backup mappe: Infinito.Nexus hemmeligheder og tokens, den selvsignerede rod CA, Let 's Kryptér konto + certifikater, ACME DNS legitimation, og node identitet (ssh host taster + machine- id). Intet af dette bor i en docker volumen, NFS eksport eller operatøren opgørelse, så det er hullet volumen / nfs backup roller ikke dækker."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A scheduled, deduplicating backup of the host’s generated secret material to the local backup directory: the Infinito.Nexus secrets and tokens, the self-signed root CA, the Let’s Encrypt account + certificates, the ACME DNS credentials, and the node identity (ssh host keys + machine-id). None of this lives in a docker volume, the NFS export or the operator inventory, so it is the gap the volume/nfs backup roles do not cover."
msgstr "En planlagt, duplikering backup af værtens genererede hemmelige materiale til den lokale backup mappe: Infinito.Nexus hemmeligheder og tokens, den selvsignerede rod CA, Let 's Kryptér konto + certifikater, ACME DNS legitimation, og node identitet (ssh host taster + machine- id). Intet af dette bor i en docker volumen, NFS eksport eller operatøren opgørelse, så det er hullet volumen / nfs backup roller ikke dækker."

msgid "A script derives the default N from RAM, CPU and free disk minus the cap sum and the 15 GB floor, with per-deploy budgets calibrated from a measured full deploy. N is overridable; its minimum is 1."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A script in this directory MUST work across every distro variant that the runner image is built for (currently Debian, Ubuntu, Arch, Fedora, CentOS). Tool availability differs across these variants, so a script SHOULD branch on `command -v <tool>` rather than on distro IDs."
msgstr "Et script i denne mappe SKAL arbejde på tværs af hver ditro variant, som runner billede er bygget til (Nuværende Debian, Ubuntu, Arch, Fedora, CentOS). Værktøjet tilgængelighed adskiller sig på tværs af disse varianter, så et script SHOVEL filial på `command -v <tool>` I stedet for distro- id 'er."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A script that is bind-mounted from this directory into a fixed in-container path (see [compose.yml](../../compose.yml)) MUST keep its git executable bit, because Docker bind-mounts preserve host file permissions and the in-container caller (systemd, dockerd, the entrypoint) cannot recover from a non-executable mount."
msgstr "Et script der er bind- monteret fra denne mappe til en fast in- container sti (Se [compose.yml](../../compose.yml)) SKAL holde sin git eksekverbar bit, fordi Docker bind- montents bevare vært filtilladelser og in-container-opkaldet (systemd, dockerd, entrypoint) kan ikke komme sig fra et ikke-eksekverbart mount."

msgid "A second instance with OpenProject, Nextcloud, Matrix, Gitea and Keycloak plays the remote live instance; it has no webhook path to the first, so every remote scenario runs in polling mode."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A second tag next to every image, which the registry cleanup then has to protect as children of the plain tag. Pushing by digest gives the same manifest list without it."
msgstr "Et andet mærke ved siden af hvert billede, som registreringsdatabasen oprydning derefter nødt til at beskytte som børn af almindelig tag. Pushing af fordøje giver den samme manifest liste uden det."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A secret denylist such as `grep -v 'password|token|key'` does **NOT** count as protection: it is case-sensitive, and secrets also travel inside URL paths. Local deploys run with `MASK_CREDENTIALS_IN_LOGS` disabled, so `no_log` does not mask these tasks."
msgstr "En hemmelig denylist såsom `grep -v 'password|token|key'` gør **IKKE** tælle som beskyttelse: Det er sagligt-følsomme, og hemmeligheder rejser også inde URL stier. Lokale programmer kører med `MASK_CREDENTIALS_IN_LOGS` deaktiveret, så `no_log` ikke skjule disse opgaver."

msgid "A secret field is locked with its value hidden, and nothing (page, log, drift report) shows the value."
msgstr ""

msgid "A secret scan runs over every snapshot before upload; a hit is redacted in the uploaded copy, and the upload goes on."
msgstr ""

msgid "A secret, a default, the order, the group and the translation key are derived, not declared. A field is secret unless it proves otherwise, fail-closed: it is non-secret only when it declares a `type` other than `password`, its `source` lies outside `users` and `secrets.credentials` and has no segment that looks like a secret or names a credential of the role's `meta/secrets.yml`, its unrendered value is a plain scalar with no template, and neither its old nor its new value holds URL userinfo or contains a credential of the role or a user's password. Its default is the resolved `source`, its order is the YAML order, its group is the form key, and its translation key is `form:<app>:<form>:<field>:label`."
msgstr ""

msgid "A selection token names a role and MAY narrow the axes that role's rows would otherwise be assigned: which variants run, which deploy mode, which node network mode, whether it runs over the WireGuard mesh, which distribution it deploys on, which filesystem its docker data root runs on and which CPU architecture it lands on. What a token leaves open stays open, exactly as an unpinned run leaves it: the priority line covers every mode and network mode the row can take, and the sweep rotation picks the distro, the filesystem and the architecture on both lines."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A selection token names a row that has to exist *on this branch* (:mod:`utils.github.variant.selection`). Nothing else in the chain can tell the operator that early: the matrix builder raises on the first bad token, one per chunk job, so a stale list costs one full CI round per entry and reports the second problem only after the first is fixed. Every problem is collected here instead, and the exit code gates the run."
msgstr "Et valg token navne en række, der skal eksistere *på denne gren* (:mod:`utils.github.variant.selection`). Intet andet i kæden kan fortælle operatøren, at tidligt: matrixbyggeren rejser på den første dårlige token, en pr chunk job, så en gammel liste koster en fuld CI runde pr post og rapporterer det andet problem først efter den første er fastsat. Hvert problem er samlet her i stedet, og exitkoden låser vejen."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A server that answers ``<source>\\n---\\n<rendering>`` passes every other rule: the rendering it appended keeps the spans, the names and the markup, and the separator is made of characters ``structure`` does not count. The reader is then served the English text as its own translation."
msgstr "En server der svarer ``<source>\\n---\\n<rendering>`` passerer enhver anden regel: den rendering det vedhæftede holder spænder, navne og markup, og separatoren er lavet af tegn ``structure`` tæller ikke. Læseren bliver derefter serveret den engelske tekst som sin egen oversættelse."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A server that gives up on a passage answers it with a label: four distinct sentences all come back as ``Name``. ``truncated`` does not see it, because its floor starts where these sources end, and every other rule passes: a label carries no span, no name, no markup and no stutter."
msgstr "En server, der giver op på en passage svarer det med en etiket: fire forskellige sætninger alle kommer tilbage som ``Name``. ``truncated`` ser det ikke, fordi dens gulv starter, hvor disse kilder slutter, og hver anden regel går: en etiket bærer ingen span, intet navn, ingen markup og ingen stammende."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A server that loses its way answers ``Cloud`` with ``Cloud Cloud Cloud``. Every other rule passes it: the spans survive, the markup count survives, it is no echo, and ``truncated`` only watches the short side."
msgstr "En server, der mister sin måde svar ``Cloud`` med ``Cloud Cloud Cloud``. Enhver anden regel går igennem den: Spans overlever, markoptælling overlever, det er ikke ekko, og ``truncated`` Kun holder øje med den korte side."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A service is a reusable dependency that an application enables via `services.<service_key>`."
msgstr "En tjeneste er en genanvendelig afhængighed, som en applikation muliggør via `services.<service_key>`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A service key is group-conditional when some role declares it with a Jinja ``enabled`` expression rather than a literal, i.e. the shape ``tests/integration/roles/meta/services/test_dynamic_flags.py`` enforces. Those keys are the ones a test deploy may drop without changing what the role under test is: their providers are co-deployed only because a host happens to be in the provider's group."
msgstr "En servicenøgle er gruppe- betinget når en rolle erklærer det med en Jinja ``enabled`` udtryk snarere end en bogstavelig, dvs. formen ``tests/integration/roles/meta/services/test_dynamic_flags.py`` håndhæver. Disse nøgler er dem en test deployering kan falde uden at ændre, hvad rolle under test er: deres udbydere er co-deployeret kun fordi en vært tilfældigvis er i udbyderens gruppe."

msgid "A service sets min_storage to a value that does not parse as a size."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A service that only ``covers:`` a capability another deployed role ``provides:`` is skipped for the same reason: it is a legacy co-tenant, the provider owns the host ports, and forwarding the co-tenant's onion ports advertises endpoints nothing answers on. The Mailu-to-Stalwart migration round deploys both, and the ports Mailu alone would serve (110, 143, 587) are dead there."
msgstr "En tjeneste, der kun ``covers:`` en kapacitet en anden indsat rolle ``provides:`` er sprunget af samme grund: Det er en arv co-lejer, udbyderen ejer værtshavnene, og videresendelse co-leaders løg havne annoncerer endepunkter intet svar på. Den Mailu-to- Stalwart migration runde iværksættes både, og havnene Mailu alene ville tjene (110, 143, 587) er døde der."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A service that spells its probe out instead of picking a flavor."
msgstr "En tjeneste, der formulerer sin sonde ud i stedet for at vælge en smag."

msgid "A services.<key> flag (``enabled`` / ``shared``) MAY be true if it is the literal Python ``True``, any string containing the substring ``in group_names``, or a string referencing a `GROUP_GATED_CONSTANTS` or `GATED_LOOKUPS` entry. Negated and compound predicates (``\"{{ 'X' not in group_names }}\"``) match on purpose: they are true on some node shape, and the static closure is the co-deploy superset. Mirrors the substring test at ``tests/integration/roles/meta/services/test_dynamic_flags.py:194``."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A shared mapper that imports every LDAP group with `preserve.group.inheritance=true` MUST NOT be used. Role names recur across applications (`administrator`, `editor`, ...) and Keycloak's `GroupTreeResolver` keys its lookup map on the group name, so the second `administrator` silently overwrites the first."
msgstr "En delt mapper, der importerer hver LDAP gruppe med `preserve.group.inheritance=true` Må ikke anvendes. Rollenavne gentages på tværs af programmer (`administrator`, `editor`,...) og Keycloaks `GroupTreeResolver` taster sin opslag kort på gruppens navn, så den anden `administrator` I tavshed overskriver den første."

msgid "A shared service other than the primary one is provided by another role."
msgstr ""

# udleder, indarbejder og integrerer. Anfør eventuelle ledsagende
# dokumentationsfiler (F.eks. `Administration.md`) Her bruger filnavn link
# tekst.
# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A short paragraph that describes what the **role** does: what it deploys, configures, and integrates. Reference any companion documentation files (e.g. `Administration.md`) here using file-name link text."
msgstr "Et kort afsnit, der beskriver **rolle** gør: hvad det udleder, indarbejder og integrerer. Anfør eventuelle ledsagende dokumentationsfiler (F.eks. `Administration.md`) Her bruger filnavn link tekst."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A short paragraph that describes what the **software** is. You MUST NOT describe what the role does here. Link the software name to its official website on first use."
msgstr "Et kort afsnit, der beskriver **software** Er. Du må ikke beskrive, hvad rollen gør her. Link software navn til sin officielle hjemmeside ved første brug."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A sidecar ``web-app-keycloak`` oauth2-proxy authenticates the visitor against Keycloak (OIDC, or LDAP federated through Keycloak) and nginx overwrites the ``X-Forwarded-*`` identity headers on every proxied request."
msgstr "En sidevogn ``web-app-keycloak`` oauth2-proxy autentificerer den besøgende mod Keycloak (OIDC, eller LDAP fødeleret gennem Keycloak) og nginx overskriver ``X-Forwarded-*`` identitetsoverskrifter på alle bekræftede anmodninger."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A sidecar `web-app-keycloak` oauth2-proxy authenticates the visitor against Keycloak (OIDC, or LDAP federated through Keycloak) and nginx overwrites the `X-Forwarded-*` identity headers on every proxied request."
msgstr "En sidevogn `web-app-keycloak` oauth2-proxy autentificerer den besøgende mod Keycloak (OIDC, eller LDAP fødeleret gennem Keycloak) og nginx overskriver `X-Forwarded-*` identitetsoverskrifter på alle bekræftede anmodninger."

msgid "A sidecar outside the workspace uploads the scanned snapshot over WebDAV at every routine checkpoint and at teardown. Start restores the latest snapshot and the `.kdbx`. Nextcloud versioning keeps earlier snapshots, so the owner can roll knowledge back."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A sidecar that a provider role ships into other stacks passes ``provider``:"
msgstr "En sidevogn, som en udbyder rolle skibe i andre stakke passerer ``provider``:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A simple and secure private infrastructure for families and small trusted groups."
msgstr "En enkel og sikker privat infrastruktur for familier og små betroede grupper."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A single OpenAI-compatible **LLM gateway** ([LiteLLM Proxy](https://docs.litellm.ai/docs/simple_proxy)) fronts every backend: local `svc-ai-ollama`, a new `svc-ai-lmstudio`, OpenRouter, and any other provider LiteLLM supports. Consumers speak only the gateway `/v1` with a model alias; provider selection and routing are gateway config. This requirement promotes the existing Flowise-local LiteLLM pattern to a shared `svc-ai-litellm` role and makes it the one place backends are declared."
msgstr "En enkelt OpenAI- kompatibel **LLM gateway** ([LiteLLM Proxy](https://docs.litellm.ai/docs/simple_proxy)) fronter hver bagende: lokal `svc-ai-ollama`, en ny `svc-ai-lmstudio`, OpenRouter, og enhver anden udbyder LiteLLM understøtter. Forbrugerne taler kun porten `/v1` med et modelalias; udbyders valg og routing er gateway config. Dette krav fremmer det eksisterende Flowise- local LiteLLM mønster til en delt `svc-ai-litellm` rolle og gør det det ene sted backends er erklæret."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A single SPOT for every service-level YAML key that is structurally incompatible with `docker stack deploy` and must therefore be omitted when IS_SWARM_MODE. Currently used for:"
msgstr "En enkelt SPOT for hver tjeneste-niveau YAML nøgle, der er strukturelt uforenelig med `docker stack deploy` og skal derfor udelades, når IS_SWARM_MODE. Anvendes i øjeblikket til:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A single YAML file's parsed root, keyed by absolute path. Every other module routes its YAML reads through here so each file is parsed at most once per process."
msgstr "En enkelt YAML fils fortolkede rod, keyed af absolut sti. Hvert andet modul ruter sin YAML læser igennem her, så hver fil er fortolket højst én gang pr. proces."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A single ``--variant`` (comma-separated, zero-based) selects the matrix rounds a run iterates: ``2`` pins one round, ``0,1,2`` is the runner-split bundle from CI discovery, empty/unset is the full matrix. One value is just a one-element bundle — there is no separate \"variants\" flag — and whether inter-round cleanup runs follows the number of selected rounds, not the flag. Centralising this here keeps init and deploy walking the exact same selection (SPOT)."
msgstr "En enkelt ``--variant`` (kommasepareret, zerobaseret) vælger matrixen runder et løb itrater: ``2`` Pins en runde, ``0,1,2`` er løber- split bundt fra CI opdagelse, tom / frakoblet er den fulde matrix. En værdi er blot en one-element bundt - der er ingen separat \"variants\" flag - og om der sker oprydning på tværs, følger antallet af valgte runder, ikke flaget. At centralisere dette her holder init og implementere walking nøjagtig samme udvalg (SPOT)."

msgid "A single `pytest` over `tests/lint`, `tests/integration` and `tests/unit` together collides on duplicate test-file basenames. Run one suite or subtree per command."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A single addon MAY be both: a `mechanism: bridge` addon MAY also declare a `bridges:` dependency on an in-repo service it relies on."
msgstr "En enkelt addon kan være begge: en `mechanism: bridge` addon MAJ også erklære en `bridges:` afhængighed af en inrepo-tjeneste, som den er afhængig af."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A single addon declaration materialised from a role's meta/addons/<id>.yml."
msgstr "En enkelt addon-erklæring fra en rolles meta / addons /<id>.yml."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A single commit (or a tight related sequence) lands the whole role addition."
msgstr "En enkelt forpligtelse (eller en tæt relateret sekvens) lander hele rollen tilføjelse."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A single commit (or a tight, related sequence) lands the whole role addition; no half-scaffolded intermediate commits."
msgstr "En enkelt forpligtelse (eller en stram, relateret sekvens) lander hele rollen tilføjelse; ingen halvstillads mellemliggende forpligtelser."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A single entry a catalog adapter surfaced for relevance + version review."
msgstr "En enkelt indgang en katalog adapter dukkede op for relevans + version gennemgang."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A single grammar covers every per-line, per-block, and per-file opt-out across the test suite. See ``docs/contributing/actions/testing/suppression.md`` for the catalog of valid rule keys, their placement, and the test that consumes each."
msgstr "En enkelt grammatik dækker hver per- linje, per- blok og per- fil opt - ud over testsuiten. Se ``docs/contributing/actions/testing/suppression.md`` for kataloget af gyldige regel nøgler, deres placering, og den test, der forbruger hver."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A single paragraph (one or two sentences) immediately below the H1. It MUST explain what kind of commands live in the directory. It MUST NOT name the sub-commands explicitly. It MUST stand on its own when extracted by the CLI help system, which collapses multi-line paragraphs into a single line."
msgstr "Et enkelt afsnit (en eller to sætninger) umiddelbart under H1. Det SKAL forklare, hvilken slags kommandoer der bor i mappen. Det SKAL IKKE navngive underkommandoerne eksplicit. Det SKAL stå alene, når det udvindes af CLI-hjælpesystemet, som kollapser multilinjens afsnit til en enkelt linje."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A single volume"
msgstr "Et enkelt volumen"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A single wildcard replaces 15+ per-shape entries (`* make *`, `docker *`, `gh api *`, `grep *`, `head *`, `tail *`, `tee *`, `wc *`, `echo *`, `pkill *`, `* > /tmp/*`, `*=* python* *`, `gh issue *`, `gh run *`, `make *`) that existed purely as workarounds for the sandbox auto-allow heuristic declining on env-prefixes, redirects, pipes, and quoted args. With `Bash(*)` the allowlist no longer rots as new command shapes emerge; the gating responsibility moves entirely to `ask` (mutating verbs) and `deny` (structurally unsafe shapes)."
msgstr "Et enkelt wildcard erstatter 15+ per- form indgange (`* make *`, `docker *`, `gh api *`, `grep *`, `head *`, `tail *`, `tee *`, `wc *`, `echo *`, `pkill *`, `* > /tmp/*`, `*=* python* *`, `gh issue *`, `gh run *`, `make *`) der eksisterede udelukkende som arbejdsområder for sandkassen auto- tillader heuristisk faldende på env- præfikser, omdirigerer, rør, og citerede buer. Med `Bash(*)` allolist ikke længere rådner som nye kommandoformer opstår; gating ansvar bevæger sig helt til `ask` (muterende verber) og `deny` (strukturelt usikre former)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A single-element list holding the expanded spec list, so the caller receives the list itself rather than its first element."
msgstr "En enkelt- element liste holder den udvidede spec liste, så den opkaldende modtager listen selv snarere end dens første element."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A single-node lab cannot answer the multi-node criteria: replica scaling, placement across two `kata-capable` Raspberry-Pi-class nodes, and the compose-plus-swarm end-to-end pass all need the cluster the requirement describes. The arm64 half of the placement criterion is proven by the image check above; the two-node half is not."
msgstr ""

msgid "A skill is Markdown. It may build on any number of routines, listed in its frontmatter as `routines`; a routine may serve several skills. A skill without routines is a pure rule skill (for example a file-type rule)."
msgstr ""

msgid "A slot belongs to a stack (D13): the allocator records each stack name with its slot in a machine registry (proposed `/var/cache/infinito/core/stacks/`, outside the cache folders, so neither eviction nor `make clean-cache` touches it). A stack keeps its slot across restarts, two stack names from one checkout get two slots, and `make worktree-up` allocates the slot of the worktree's default stack name. Phase 8 retires the slots for deploys once the pool's live proof is recorded."
msgstr ""

msgid "A slot belongs to a stack, not to a checkout."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A small Express middleware (``files/sso/header_auth.js``, mounted into ``server.js`` at build time by ``files/sso/patch_server.js``) reads only those nginx-overwritten ``X-Forwarded-*`` headers and flips ``req.session.loggedIn = true``, so the existing ``isAuthenticated`` gate on ``/admin`` opens for the proxied owner."
msgstr "Et lille Express mellemstykke (``files/sso/header_auth.js``, monteret i ``server.js`` på byggetid af ``files/sso/patch_server.js``) læser kun dem nginx- overskrevet ``X-Forwarded-*`` hovedbeklædning og flips ``req.session.loggedIn = true``, så den eksisterende ``isAuthenticated`` gate on ``/admin`` Åbner for den fuldkomne ejer."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A small Express middleware (`files/sso/header_auth.js`, mounted into `server.js` at build time by `files/sso/patch_server.js`) reads only those nginx-overwritten `X-Forwarded-*` headers and flips `req.session.loggedIn = true`, so the existing `isAuthenticated` gate on `/admin` opens for the proxied owner."
msgstr "Et lille Express mellemstykke (`files/sso/header_auth.js`, monteret i `server.js` på byggetid af `files/sso/patch_server.js`) læser kun dem nginx- overskrevet `X-Forwarded-*` hovedbeklædning og flips `req.session.loggedIn = true`, så den eksisterende `isAuthenticated` gate on `/admin` Åbner for den fuldkomne ejer."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A small SMTP relay that carries `.onion` recipients over Tor. The active mail provider (Stalwart) cannot open a SOCKS connection of its own, and a `.onion` address cannot be reached any other way, so the provider hands every `.onion` recipient to this gateway as an ordinary SMTP relay target and the gateway dials `<recipient-domain>:25` through Tor's SOCKS5 listener."
msgstr "En lille SMTP relæ, der bærer `.onion` modtagere over Tor. Den aktive postudbyder (Stalwart Formand) kan ikke åbne sin egen SOCKS-forbindelse, og `.onion` adresse kan ikke nås nogen anden måde, så udbyderen hænder hver `.onion` modtager til denne gateway som et almindeligt SMTP relæ mål og gateway ringer `<recipient-domain>:25` gennem Tors SOCKS5 Lytter."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A small SMTP relay that carries ``.onion`` recipients over Tor. The active mail provider (Stalwart) cannot open a SOCKS connection of its own, and a ``.onion`` address cannot be reached any other way, so the provider hands every ``.onion`` recipient to this gateway as an ordinary SMTP relay target and the gateway dials ``<recipient-domain>:25`` through Tor’s SOCKS5 listener."
msgstr "En lille SMTP relæ, der bærer ``.onion`` modtagere over Tor. Den aktive postudbyder (Stalwart Formand) kan ikke åbne sin egen SOCKS-forbindelse, og ``.onion`` adresse kan ikke nås nogen anden måde, så udbyderen hænder hver ``.onion`` modtager til denne gateway som et almindeligt SMTP relæ mål og gateway ringer ``<recipient-domain>:25`` gennem Tors SOCKS5 Lytter."

