msgstr "Et eksempel på, hvordan du bruger denne rolle i din spillebog:"

msgid "An explicit `network` input still wins over the full coverage: `clearnet`, `tor` and `multi` are operator narrowings. A variant that pins `services.tor.enabled` to false only ever runs on clearnet regardless, and so does a role without a `tor` bond unless its deploy pulls the Tor provider in, which adds `multi`."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "An explicit per-domain allowlist is required because the wildcard form `WebFetch(domain:*)` is **inert**: observed empirically, the permission prompt still fires for every new host despite the wildcard being present, so the wildcard buys nothing. Contributors who need a new origin MUST extend this list (and the sandbox `allowedDomains` in [sandbox.md](sandbox.md)) explicitly."
msgstr "En eksplicit per- domæne allolist er påkrævet, fordi wildcard formular `WebFetch(domain:*)` er **inert**: observeret empirisk, tilladelse prompte stadig brande for hver ny vært trods wildcard er til stede, så wildcard køber intet. Bidragydere, der har brug for en ny oprindelse SKAL udvide denne liste (og sandkassen `allowedDomains` til [sandbox.md](sandbox.md)) eksplicit."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "An explicit string value at applications['web-app-nextcloud'] .services.sso.oidc.plugin (inventory override)."
msgstr "En eksplicit strengværdi ved programmer['web-app-nextcloud'] .services.sso.oidc.plugin (Overskridelse af lagerstatus)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "An expression combines ids with ``AND`` and ``OR``. ``AND`` means every licence applies at once, so the strictest wins: grants intersect, duties and disclaimers union. ``OR`` means the licensee picks one whole licence, so the alternative with the most favourable context wins and its own row is used. Folding ``OR`` field by field would invent a licence nobody offers: Redis under ``AGPL-3.0-only OR RSALv2 OR SSPL-1.0`` would come out carrying no duty at all, because no single duty is common to all three."
msgstr "Et udtryk kombinerer id med ``AND`` og ``OR``. ``AND`` betyder enhver licens gælder på én gang, så de strengeste vinder: giver intersect, pligter og ansvarsfraskrivelse union. ``OR`` licenstageren vælger en hel licens, så alternativet med den gunstigste kontekst vinder, og dens egen række anvendes. Foldning ``OR`` felt for felt ville opfinde en licens ingen tilbyder: Redis under ``AGPL-3.0-only OR RSALv2 OR SSPL-1.0`` Jeg vil gerne sige, at vi ikke har nogen pligt, for der er ingen fælles pligt for alle tre."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "An image build reaches the cache by hostname, but it cannot verify the frontend's self-signed certificate unless its Dockerfile installs the CA, so only these are safe to hijack for every build. A build that does install the CA additionally gets the TLS hosts; `sys-svc-compose`'s override generator decides that per image."
msgstr "Et billede build når cachen ved værtsnavn, men det kan ikke kontrollere frontend 's selvsignerede certifikat, medmindre dens Dockerfile installerer CA, så kun disse er sikre at kapre for hver bygning. En bygning, der installerer CA desuden får TLS værter; `sys-svc-compose`Det bestemmer generatoren pr. billede."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "An in-house theme carries a variable mapping natively (see [web-app-gitea](../../../../../roles/web-app-gitea/templates/theme.css.j2)). The role stylesheet maps the app's CSS variables onto the tokens only for what no in-house option reaches."
msgstr "Et in-house tema bærer en variabel kortlægning indbygget (Se [web-app-gitea](../../../../../roles/web-app-gitea/templates/theme.css.j2)). Rollestylesheet kortlægger appens CSS variabler på tokens kun for, hvad ingen in-house mulighed når."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "An incomplete read can only ever overstate the capability, because the intersection skips what it could not see. A caller may therefore trust ``capability`` to decide an architecture is missing, but must not conclude from it that a narrowing is unnecessary while ``unread`` is non-empty: the image it could not read may be the one the narrowing exists for."
msgstr "En ufuldstændig læsning kan kun overvurdere evnen, fordi skæringspunktet springer over, hvad det ikke kunne se. En ringer kan derfor stole på ``capability`` at beslutte en arkitektur mangler, men må ikke konkludere fra det, at en indsnævring er unødvendig, mens ``unread`` er ikke-tom: det billede, det ikke kunne læse, kan være det, indsnævringen findes for."

