# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Inference requests exhaust the container limits `mem_limit: 256m` and `cpus: \"0.2\"` of `meta/services.yml`, because gunicorn starts four workers (`LT_THREADS` default) that each load the models on their first request. Measured: three `POST /translate` calls in a row gave `502` after 4.7 s, `200` after 79 s and `502` after 40 s with four `Worker (pid) was sent SIGKILL! Perhaps out of memory?` lines, and a series of `POST /detect` calls from Swagger UI (at most sixteen) killed two more workers and left the container at 248.9 MiB of 256 MiB and 20 % CPU, reported `healthy`, while no request (not even a static file) was answered for 20 minutes until the container was restarted. Options: raise `mem_limit` and `cpus`, set `LT_THREADS` to one worker in `templates/env.j2`, and let `scripts/healthcheck.py` fail when the HTTP port stops answering."
msgstr "Inferens anmoder om udstødning af beholderens grænser `mem_limit: 256m` og `cpus: \"0.2\"` af `meta/services.yml`, fordi gunicorn starter fire arbejdere (`LT_THREADS` standard) at hver indlæser modellerne på deres første anmodning. Målt: tre `POST /translate` opkald i træk givet `502` efter 4.7 s `200` efter 79 s og `502` efter 40 s med fire `Worker (pid) was sent SIGKILL! Perhaps out of memory?` linjer og en række `POST /detect` opkald fra Swagger UI (højst 16) Dræbte to arbejdere mere og forlod containeren ved 248.9 MIB af 256 MiB og 20 % CPU, rapporteret `healthy`, mens ingen anmodning (ikke engang en statisk fil) blev besvaret for 20 minutter indtil beholderen blev genstartet. Indstillinger: raise `mem_limit` og `cpus`, set `LT_THREADS` til én arbejdstager i `templates/env.j2`, og lad `scripts/healthcheck.py` mislykkes, når HTTP- porten stopper med at svare."

