msgid "No Playwright scenario gates on `ldap`, and [`templates/playwright.env.j2`](./templates/playwright.env.j2) suppresses the service-gate check for `LDAP_SERVICE_ENABLED`. Shopware has no LDAP sign-in of its own and the role installs no admin-LDAP extension, so there is no LDAP-bind surface to drive: with `sso` on, directory accounts reach the administration through Keycloak's user federation and the AdminOpenAuth provider, which [`files/playwright/test-rbac.js`](./files/playwright/test-rbac.js) covers; with `sso` off, no directory account reaches Shopware."
msgstr ""

msgid "No Playwright scenario gates on `ldap`, and [services.yml](./meta/services.yml) exempts the flag from the Playwright service-flag check. The indexer configures LDAP only as `ldap_authz_domain`, which adds `backend_roles` to a user Keycloak or `internal_users.yml` already authenticated, so the stack has no LDAP-bind login to drive: with `sso` on every directory account signs in through Keycloak, which [files/playwright/test-rbac-roles.js](./files/playwright/test-rbac-roles.js) covers, and with `sso` off only the internal `admin` and `kibanaserver` accounts can sign in."
msgstr ""

msgid "No Playwright scenario proves `GITEA__admin__EXTERNAL_USER_DISABLE_FEATURES`: Gitea enforces it on the settings pages only, not on `PATCH /api/v1/user/settings` (read from `routers/api/v1/user/settings.go`). Options: sign biber in through Keycloak and assert the disabled full-name field on `/user/settings`."
msgstr ""

msgid "No Playwright scenario proves that the LDAP bind password stays out of the deploy log and the process list of the node: `tasks/setup/ldap.yml` now hands it to `gitea admin auth add-ldap` and `update-ldap` through the environment, and a browser cannot observe either surface. Options: a role-local integration test that renders `GITEA_LDAP_AUTH_ARGS` and asserts the credential is absent."
msgstr ""

msgid "No Playwright scenario proves the LDAP avatar (`jpegPhoto`) or the LDAP quota (`nextcloudQuota`): no persona carries either attribute, Keycloak exposes no photo upload, and both reach Nextcloud only through `processAttributes` (first item). Options: seed both attributes on `biber` in the directory fixture and assert them after a native LDAP login."
msgstr ""

msgid "No Playwright scenario proves the LDAP avatar: no persona carries `jpegPhoto`, and Gitea uploads the LDAP avatar only when it creates the account or syncs it. Options: seed `jpegPhoto` on `biber` in the directory fixture and assert a non-default `avatar_url`."
msgstr ""

msgid "No Playwright scenario proves the OIDC source's group claim, admin group, restricted group or `GITEA__oauth2_client__USERNAME`: the personas now sign in through the OAuth source (`ACCOUNT_LINKING=auto`), but no spec reads the admin or restricted flag of the account they land on. Options: a scenario that signs biber in through Keycloak while holding the administrator role group and asserts the admin badge in the navbar."
msgstr ""

msgid "No Playwright spec edits an entry through phpLDAPadmin, so the write access the `svc-db-openldap` ACL grants the `web-app-phpldapadmin` administrator group is asserted only through the equivalent `web-app-lam` clause (`roles/web-app-lam/files/playwright/test-directory-login.js`). Cause: the role is end of life and outside every CI round, and its v2 entry editor is a JavaScript form no spec drives yet. Options: add an edit spec when the role returns to a CI lifecycle."
msgstr ""

msgid "No Playwright test proves that a member gets the admin flag: the only administrator with a Pixelfed account is the artisan administrator, whom both `files/python/rbac_sync.py` and the sign-in listener `files/php/rbac/oidc_login.php` skip, so `files/playwright/test-rbac-admin-flag.js` can only prove that no non-member holds the flag, and `files/playwright/test-oidc-login-biber.js` runs the listener only for a non-member that never held the flag. Options: an inventory persona granted `administrator` on Pixelfed, then a spec that signs it in through OIDC and asserts its admin badge in that session."
