msgid "That baseline is narrower than the truth. Its closure follows `run_after`, dependency and service edges, so a cross-role Jinja include is covered only where such an edge matches, and a renamed role path seeds only the new role. The plan lists changed paths with rename detection off, so a move counts both its old and its new path."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "That choice is wrong in two directions at once. A prompt that needs a large context window reaches a model that cannot hold it, which is how [`web-app-hermes`](../../roles/web-app-hermes/) answers HTTP 500 when the agent model declares fewer than 64000 tokens. And a one-line factual question reaches whatever the deploy happened to pick, which is usually the largest model available."
msgstr "Dette valg er forkert i to retninger på én gang. En prompt, der har brug for en stor kontekst vindue når en model, der ikke kan holde det, hvilket er, hvordan [`web-app-hermes`](../../roles/web-app-hermes/) svar på HTTP 500 når agentmodellen erklærer færre end 64000 Poletter. Og et one- line faktuel spørgsmål når uanset hvilken implementering der skete at vælge, som normalt er den største model til rådighed."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "That contract is wrong for one class of failure. When a value could not be measured and substituting one would be a guess, silence turns a loud stop into a wrong number nobody sees. Such a failure raises from here and every render layer re-raises it untouched."
msgstr "Denne kontrakt er forkert for én klasse af fiasko. Når en værdi ikke kunne måles og erstatte en ville være et gæt, stilhed vender et højt stop til et forkert nummer ingen ser. En sådan fiasko rejser sig herfra, og hver gør lag re- hæver det uberørt."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "That file brings the client to its desired MCP state from scratch, so the same file serves the role's own run and this one. `tests/lint/ansible/services/test_mcp_client_entrypoint.py` fails when a client role lacks it."
msgstr "Denne fil bringer kunden til sin ønskede MCP tilstand fra bunden, så den samme fil tjener rollens egen køre og denne ene. `tests/lint/ansible/services/test_mcp_client_entrypoint.py` mislykkes, når en klient rolle mangler det."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "That file brings the client to its desired MCP state from scratch, so the same file serves the role’s own run and this one. ``tests/lint/ansible/services/test_mcp_client_entrypoint.py`` fails when a client role lacks it."
msgstr "Denne fil bringer kunden til sin ønskede MCP tilstand fra bunden, så den samme fil tjener rollens egen køre og denne ene. ``tests/lint/ansible/services/test_mcp_client_entrypoint.py`` mislykkes, når en klient rolle mangler det."

msgid "That is also what a retrigger replays: `--failed` reads the glyphs off the failed job's title and writes them back as a token, so the row comes back in the mode, network mode, distribution and architecture it died on rather than on whatever the rotation would pick next. The architecture is replayed because it is the machine the job ran on, not a preference it could fall back from. The filesystem is deliberately left out. A title states the kind the matrix *assigned*, which a deploy is allowed to fall back from, so pinning it would both misstate what the job ran on and turn the kind into a demand, failing the retrigger on the very condition the fallback absorbs."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "That is what stops the supervisor flow rather than effort. Flowise reaches an MCP server over the container network, and a stdio server has no address there: the client spawns and owns the process, so a shared endpoint two consumers could hold at once does not exist, and the deploy-time contract probe would consume the only session. Wrapping each agent in a stdio-to-HTTP bridge would put an unreviewed process on the platform's most privileged path — an agent with tool access — to work around a transport upstream has not shipped, which is the workaround this project refuses. Re-review when either upstream serves MCP over HTTP."
msgstr "Det er det, der forhindrer vejlederen i at flyde i stedet for at gøre en indsats. Flowise når en MCP-server over containernetværket, og en stdio-server har ingen adresse der: klienten spår og ejer processen, så en delt endpoint to forbrugere kunne holde på én gang ikke eksisterer, og deploy- time kontrakt sonden ville forbruge den eneste session. Indpakning hver agent i en stdio- to- HTTP bro ville sætte en urevideret proces på platformens mest privilegerede vej - en agent med værktøjsadgang - til at arbejde omkring en transport opstrøms ikke har afsendt, hvilket er arbejdet omkring dette projekt nægter. Re- gennemgang, når enten opstrøms tjener MCP over HTTP."

