# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The filer page runs its own inline script (it defines `reportProgress` for the upload progress bar) and inline event handlers, but `meta/csp.yml` grants neither `script-src-elem` nor `script-src-attr`. They run only because `build_csp_header` (`plugins/filter/csp_filters.py`) adds `'unsafe-inline'` to both directives whenever the `logout` service is enabled. With `logout` disabled the browser refuses them (\"Executing inline script violates ... script-src-elem\", \"Executing inline event handler violates ... script-src-attr\"), the upload progress never renders, and the design spec \"the upload progress bar is the primary fill and carries its on-color\" fails. Options: grant the filer's script needs in `meta/csp.yml` (flags for both directives, or hashes of the upstream snippets per pinned version), or let the filer page carry its own policy."
msgstr "Filersiden kører sit eget inline script (det definerer `reportProgress` for upload- statuslinjen) og inline event handlere, men `meta/csp.yml` tilskud `script-src-elem` eller `script-src-attr`. De løber kun fordi `build_csp_header` (`plugins/filter/csp_filters.py`) tilføjer `'unsafe-inline'` til begge direktiver, når `logout` service er aktiveret. Med `logout` deaktiveret browseren nægter dem (\"Udførelse inline script overtræder... script- src- elem\", \"Udførelse inline event handler overtræder... script- src- attr\"), upload fremskridt aldrig gør, og design spec \"upload statuslinjen er den primære fyld og bærer sin on- farve\" mislykkes. Indstillinger: give filens script behov i `meta/csp.yml` (flag for begge direktiver, eller hash af opstrøms snuppets pr fastspændt version), eller lade filsiden bære sin egen politik."

