# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The list below was produced by grepping each `roles/<role>/files/playwright/playwright.spec.js` for `biber|BIBER`. A role appears under \"missing\" iff it has a Playwright spec, no biber references, AND its policy classification (next column) says one is expected. Each checkbox MUST be closed by reading the spec end to end, deciding whether the role is in scope, and then either adding the biber scenario (and the env keys) OR documenting in the commit message why the role is exempt and removing it from this list."
msgstr "Nedenstående liste blev udarbejdet ved at fedte hver `roles/<role>/files/playwright/playwright.spec.js` til `biber|BIBER`. En rolle vises under \"missing\" iff det har en Playwright spec, ingen biber referencer, OG dens politik klassificering (næste kolonne) siger, at der forventes en. Hvert afkrydsningsfelt SKAL lukkes ved at læse spec enden til slut, afgøre om rollen er i rækkevidde, og derefter enten tilføje biber scenario (og env tasterne) OR dokumenterer i commitmeddelelsen, hvorfor rollen er undtaget og fjerner den fra denne liste."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The list below was produced by grepping each role's `meta/services.yml` for an `ldap` block with `enabled` set to something other than `false`. Each checkbox MUST be closed by reading the spec end to end, deciding whether the role exposes a test-drivable LDAP auth surface, and then either adding the LDAP scenario OR documenting in the commit message why the role is exempt (e.g. the LDAP integration is consumer-side only, with no Playwright- reachable login UI)."
msgstr "Listen nedenfor blev udarbejdet ved at greppe hver rolles `meta/services.yml` til en `ldap` blok med `enabled` indstillet til noget andet end `false`. Hvert afkrydsningsfelt SKAL lukkes ved at læse spec slutningen til slutningen, afgøre, om rollen udsætter en test- driverbar LDAP auth overflade, og derefter enten tilføje LDAP scenario ELLER dokumentere i commit message hvorfor rollen er fritaget (fx LDAP integration er forbruger-side kun, uden Playwright- adgang login UI)."

