msgstr "Kortet selv er genereret, aldrig sporet, så ingen anden kopi af et værtsnavn kan drive; ``utils.cache.render.render_artifacts`` skriver det, når værdisættet er bygget."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The map of which role wires in which is derived from the roles themselves on every docs build, by [infinito_docs/generators/integrations.py](../../roles/web-app-docs/files/python/infinito_docs/generators/integrations.py), and reached from [docs/architecture/integrations.rst](../architecture/integrations.rst). Its two sources are the declarations this requirement governs: a **wired** edge comes from a top-level service key in the row role's `meta/services.yml`, and a **declared** edge from the `bridges:` entry of a `meta/addons/*.yml`. Edges are directional — the row hosts the flag or the plugin — so a bidirectional pair such as `nextcloud`↔`openproject` appears twice. It currently covers 98 roles with **811 wired edges plus 99 bridged addon edges**."
msgstr "Kortet over hvilken rolle ledninger, som er afledt af rollerne selv på hver docs bygge, ved [infinito_docs/generators/integrations.py](../../roles/web-app-docs/files/python/infinito_docs/generators/integrations.py), og nået fra [docs/architecture/integrations.rst](../architecture/integrations.rst). Dens to kilder er de erklæringer, som dette krav gælder: **tilkoblet** kant kommer fra en top-niveau service nøgle i rækken rollens `meta/services.yml`, og **anmeldt** kant fra `bridges:` entry of a `meta/addons/*.yml`. Kanter er retningsbestemte - rækken er vært for flag eller plugin - så en tovejs par såsom `nextcloud`↔`openproject` vises to gange. Den dækker i øjeblikket 98 roller med **811 kablede kanter plus 99 Forgrenede addonkanter**."

msgid "The marked row carries `instructions: <mode>` in the matrix JSON, and the plan table names that mode in its 📖 column; its job title is that of an ordinary deploy row."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The marker adds `web-app-docs` to that row's `apps`, so the documentation is deployed beside the role under test. Its own CLI test then reads the role's page, takes the Production block out of the rendered HTML, and runs it."
msgstr "Markøren tilføjer `web-app-docs` til den række `apps`, så dokumentationen er indsat ved siden af den rolle, der testes. Dens egen CLI test derefter læser rollens side, tager produktionen blok ud af den afleverede HTML, og kører det."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The marker file carries the same name as the swarm drill's (`scripts/tests/deploy/swarm/routine/backup/base.sh`) — one name for one concept. The implementations stay apart on purpose: the swarm drill follows a single token across five hops on four machines from the controller, which has nothing in common with marking every subject of one host beyond the three lines that write a file and read it back."
msgstr "Markørfilen bærer samme navn som sværmboret. (`scripts/tests/deploy/swarm/routine/backup/base.sh`) - et navn for et koncept. Implementeringerne holdes adskilt med vilje: sværmboret følger en enkelt token på tværs af fem humle på fire maskiner fra controlleren, som ikke har noget til fælles med at markere hvert emne af en vært ud over de tre linjer, der skriver en fil og læse den tilbage."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The marker is a comment, so it never reaches the merged services map or `host_vars`. It applies only to the variant entry it stands in; the same role's other variants are unaffected. A primary app keeps the index the sweep assigned it and no pin overrides it."
msgstr "Markøren er en kommentar, så det aldrig når den fusionerede tjenester kort eller `host_vars`. Det gælder kun for den variant, det står i; den samme rolles andre varianter er upåvirket. En primær app holder indekset den feje tildelt det og ingen pin tilsidesætter det."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The marker lives beside the pins that cause the overage, so it is visible to whoever edits them, and it is registered as a rule in [suppression.md](../../../../../docs/contributing/actions/testing/suppression.md) like every other suppression. It expires on its own: `test_every_mem_limit_exemption_is_still_needed` fails once the marked variant fits again, so it cannot outlive the cause it was written for. Add one only when no variant placement brings the footprint under the cap, and record in the text which placements were tried."
msgstr "Markøren lever ved siden af de stifter, der forårsager overforbrug, så det er synligt for den, der redigerer dem, og det er registreret som en regel i [suppression.md](../../../../../docs/contributing/actions/testing/suppression.md) som enhver anden undertrykkelse. Den udløber på egen hånd: `test_every_mem_limit_exemption_is_still_needed` mislykkes når den markerede variant passer igen, så det kan ikke overleve den årsag, det blev skrevet for. Tilføj kun en, når ingen variant placering bringer fodaftryk under hætten, og registrere i teksten, hvilke placeringer blev prøvet."

msgid "The marker lives outside the stack and its volumes, so it survives ``docker stack rm``, ``docker compose down``, a crashed database and the stop and start cycle of ``backup.project_hard_restart``. A host that carries the marker therefore redeploys while its dedicated database is down, as in the restore of ```svc-bkp-nfs-2-local`` <../svc-bkp-nfs-2-local/README.md>`__ (``docker stack rm``, restore, redeploy). A dedicated store on a host without the marker, such as a 0.16 host or a host whose instance directory was lost, needs its database running before the deploy: start the database service of the stack the host last deployed, then deploy. Before a host that carries the marker goes back to a 0.16 store, through ``stalwart-migrate rollback`` or a backup taken under 0.16, delete the marker, so the next deploy reads the store."
msgstr ""

msgid "The marker lives outside the stack and its volumes, so it survives `docker stack rm`, `docker compose down`, a crashed database and the stop and start cycle of `backup.project_hard_restart`. A host that carries the marker therefore redeploys while its dedicated database is down, as in the restore of [`svc-bkp-nfs-2-local`](../svc-bkp-nfs-2-local/README.md) (`docker stack rm`, restore, redeploy). A dedicated store on a host without the marker, such as a 0.16 host or a host whose instance directory was lost, needs its database running before the deploy: start the database service of the stack the host last deployed, then deploy. Before a host that carries the marker goes back to a 0.16 store, through `stalwart-migrate rollback` or a backup taken under 0.16, delete the marker, so the next deploy reads the store."
msgstr ""

msgid "The marker names the directory it was placed as, so a copy of a placed role under another name, which carries the same file, never counts as placed. It is written and read without following a symbolic link."
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid "The marker sits on the construct's own line or on any line of the comment block directly above it, Jinja ``{# #}`` or ``#``."
msgstr ""

msgid "The marker sits on the definition's line or in the comment block above it, and answers every read through that name and through the names derived from it."
msgstr ""

msgid "The marker that identifies a custom role the pull placed under ``roles/``."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The match stream is built once per process by `_scan.iter_matches` and shared across the four test classes; the repo-derived context (application defaults, user defaults, per-role schemas, `application_id`-declaring role set) comes from `_scan.get_context`. Validation helpers live in `_validate.py`. Suppression is wired through the project's `noqa` / `nocheck` grammar; the rule key is `lookup-config-path` (see [suppression.md](../../../../../docs/contributing/actions/testing/suppression.md))."
msgstr "Matchstrømmen er bygget en gang pr. proces ved `_scan.iter_matches` og delt på tværs af de fire testklasser; den repoafledte kontekst (applikationsstandard, brugerstandard, perrolleskema `application_id`-erklære rolle sæt) kommer fra `_scan.get_context`. Validering hjælpere lever i `_validate.py`. Undertrykkelse er forbundet gennem projektets `noqa` / `nocheck` grammatik; regelnøglen er `lookup-config-path` (Se [suppression.md](../../../../../docs/contributing/actions/testing/suppression.md))."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The matcher itself lives in :mod:`utils.cache.gitignore` (single SPOT for ``.gitignore`` parsing and matching). :func:`iter_non_ignored_files` here composes the cached project walk with that matcher and is the recommended helper for lint tests that want the \"files git would track\" view without subprocessing."
msgstr "Selve matcheren bor i :mod:`utils.cache.gitignore` (enkelt SPOT for ``.gitignore`` parsing og matching). :func:`iter_non_ignored_files` her komponerer caching projekt gå med at matcher og er den anbefalede hjælper til flint test, der ønsker \"filer git ville spore\" visning uden underbehandling."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The materialised application payload exposes services under the bare ``services`` key (no ``compose.services`` wrapper). The function name is preserved for backwards compatibility with existing call sites."
msgstr "Den materialiserede anvendelse nyttelast udsætter tjenester under bare ``services`` nøgle (ng ``compose.services`` papir). Funktionsnavnet bevares for baglæns kompatibilitet med eksisterende opkaldssteder."

msgid "The matrix and survey backlog (the per-role upstream-plugin survey, wiring every open cell, gating integration addons on their partner, opt-in paid cells, reconciling already-wired plugins, the cross-role integration specs and the SSO cells) moved to the acceptance criteria of [027](027-integration-matrix.md)."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The matrix hands every row exactly one filesystem, so the value a deploy job sees is always narrow. Reading that narrowness as a demand would turn every condition the applying step is built to tolerate into a red row: a loop device it could not claim, a pool another job still holds, a kernel without the module."
msgstr "Den matrix hænder hver række præcis én filsystem, så værdien en implementering job ser er altid smal. At læse, at smalhed som et krav ville vende enhver betingelse det anvendte trin er bygget til at tolerere i en rød række: en løkke enhed, det ikke kunne hævde, en pool et andet job stadig holder, en kerne uden modulet."

msgid "The matrix orchestrator (`utils/tests/swarm/matrix.py`) drives the deploy stage per variant round; `routine/00_one.sh` drives the surrounding stages for one distro, and the workflow `.github/workflows/call-test-deploy.yml` drives the distro loop. Run one app locally with `make swarm-zombie app=<id>` or the whole matrix via `make roundtrip`. Both copy the rescue bundle to the host through `utils/release.sh` and then release the cluster; `keep=true` keeps it for inspection."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The matrix orchestrator needs these before it provisions, so that the authorized_keys reach host_vars through the merging ``--vars`` channel rather than through the replacing extra-vars file."
msgstr "Den matrix orkestrator har brug for disse, før det leverer, så authorized_keys rækkevidde host_vars gennem fusioneringen ``--vars`` kanal snarere end gennem den erstatter ekstravars fil."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The matrix-variant planner (see [variants.md](variants.md)) calls the expansion once per round, so each round's inventory gets the right transitive closure for that round's variant set."
msgstr "Matrix- variantplanlæggeren (Se [variants.md](variants.md)) kalder udvidelse en gang per runde, så hver rundes opgørelse får den rigtige transitive lukning for den rundes variant sæt."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The mautrix network bridges are declared in ``meta/addons/`` as ``mechanism: bridge`` addons (requirement 026, Decision 13). Each is ``required: false`` and **disabled by default**; its per-network DB password and its appservice ``as_token``/``hs_token`` pair are referenced from ```meta/secrets.yml`` <./meta/secrets.yml>`__ ``credentials:``, never inlined. The role renders each bridge’s ``config.yaml`` and the matching Synapse ``registration.yaml`` from the same tokens."
msgstr "De mautrix netværk broer er erklæret i ``meta/addons/`` som ``mechanism: bridge`` addons (krav 026, afgørelse 13). Hver er ``required: false`` og **deaktiveret som standard**; dens password for menunetværk DB og dens appservice ``as_token``/``hs_token`` par er refereret fra ```meta/secrets.yml`` <./meta/secrets.yml>`__ ``credentials:``, never inlined. The role renders each bridge’s ``config.yaml`` and the matching Synapse ``registration.yaml`` fra de samme tokens."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The mautrix network bridges are declared in `meta/addons/` as `mechanism: bridge` addons (requirement 026, Decision 13). Each is `required: false` and **disabled by default**; its per-network DB password and its appservice `as_token`/`hs_token` pair are referenced from [`meta/secrets.yml`](./meta/secrets.yml) `credentials:`, never inlined. The role renders each bridge's `config.yaml` and the matching Synapse `registration.yaml` from the same tokens."
