# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The role comes from ``APP_ID``, which the deploy workflow sets to the row's app and :mod:`cli.administration.deploy.development.deploy.run` forwards into the container. A round that carries no such name, or one naming a role that publishes no guide, draws an invokable peer at random instead, so a local round covers a different guide each time rather than always the first one the inventory happens to list. Invokability comes from :func:`utils.roles.validation.invokable.list_invokable_app_ids`, so no caller re-derives it from role-name prefixes."
msgstr "Rollen kommer fra ``APP_ID``, som deployering workflow sætter til rækken app og :mod:`cli.administration.deploy.development.deploy.run` Fremad ind i beholderen. En runde, der ikke bærer et sådant navn, eller en navngivning en rolle, der udgiver ingen vejledning, trækker en uovervindelig peer på tilfældig i stedet, så en lokal runde dækker en anden guide hver gang i stedet for altid den første, som opgørelsen sker til liste. Invokability kommer fra :func:`utils.roles.validation.invokable.list_invokable_app_ids`, så ingen ringer re- stammer det fra role- navn præfikser."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The role configures a systemd service and timer which executes the CSP crawler periodically against all NGINX domains."
msgstr "Rollen er en systemd service og timer, der udfører CSP kravler regelmæssigt mod alle NGINX domæner."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The role configures and deploys a containerized PhpMyAdmin instance using Docker Compose. It optionally integrates with a central database and uses dynamic Ansible variables to support flexible deployments in both production and homelab environments."
msgstr "Rollen er og implementerer en containerized PhpMyAdmin instans, der bruger Docker ComposeDen integrerer eventuelt med en central database og bruger dynamiske Anible variabler til at understøtte fleksible installationer i både produktions- og homelab-miljøer."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The role creates no `Decidim::System::Admin`, so the system panel behind `/system/admins/sign_in` has no account in the `production` environment; in the `development` environment the upstream seed creates `system@example.org` (measured: one system administrator on the compose stack). The design spec therefore covers the sign-in page of the panel only. Options: create the system administrator from the platform administrator in `tasks/01_setup.yml` with the password on stdin, then extend `files/playwright/test-design.js` by the panel views."
msgstr "Den rolle skaber ingen `Decidim::System::Admin`, så systemet panel bag `/system/admins/sign_in` har ingen konto i `production` - miljø `development` miljø opstrømsfrø skaber `system@example.org` (målt: en systemadministrator på komponentstakken). Designet spec derfor dækker signal- i siden af panelet. Indstillinger: oprette systemadministratoren fra platformen administrator i `tasks/01_setup.yml` med adgangskoden på stdin, derefter udvide `files/playwright/test-design.js` af panelets synspunkter."

msgid "The role declares its resources for the 600M checkpoint. A larger one needs ``mem_reservation``, ``mem_limit`` and ``min_storage`` of ``meta/services.yml`` raised with it."
msgstr ""

msgid "The role declares its resources for the 600M checkpoint. A larger one needs `mem_reservation`, `mem_limit` and `min_storage` of `meta/services.yml` raised with it."
msgstr ""

msgid "The role declares no single npm pin for the Codex CLI."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The role declares no volume: a kernel that executes code a chat wrote gets a fresh filesystem on every restart. A consumer reaches it as ``http://jupyter:8888`` once it declares ``jupyter`` in its own ``meta/services.yml`` with ``enabled`` and ``shared`` set. ``web-app-openwebui`` ships that flag and sends ``CODE_EXECUTION_ENGINE=jupyter`` with it."
msgstr "Rollen erklærer ingen volumen: en kerne, der udfører kode en chat skrev får en frisk filsystem på hver genstart. En forbruger når det som ``http://jupyter:8888`` når det erklærer ``jupyter`` i sin egen ``meta/services.yml`` med ``enabled`` og ``shared`` sæt. ``web-app-openwebui`` skibe, der fører og sender ``CODE_EXECUTION_ENGINE=jupyter`` med det."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The role declares no volume: a kernel that executes code a chat wrote gets a fresh filesystem on every restart. A consumer reaches it as `http://jupyter:8888` once it declares `jupyter` in its own `meta/services.yml` with `enabled` and `shared` set. `web-app-openwebui` ships that flag and sends `CODE_EXECUTION_ENGINE=jupyter` with it."
msgstr "Rollen erklærer ingen volumen: en kerne, der udfører kode en chat skrev får en frisk filsystem på hver genstart. En forbruger når det som `http://jupyter:8888` når det erklærer `jupyter` i sin egen `meta/services.yml` med `enabled` og `shared` sæt. `web-app-openwebui` skibe, der fører og sender `CODE_EXECUTION_ENGINE=jupyter` med det."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The role deploys a single ``registry:2`` instance in pull-through proxy mode on its inventory group’s host. Because the group typically holds exactly one host (the swarm manager), ``DEPLOYMENT_MODE`` resolves to ``compose`` for the role; multi-host fan-out for the cache itself is out of scope for v1."
msgstr "Den rolle, som en enkelt ``registry:2`` tilfælde i pull- through proxy mode på sin beholdning gruppens vært. Fordi gruppen typisk har præcis én vært (sværmbestyrer), ``DEPLOYMENT_MODE`` Beslutter ``compose`` for rollen; multi-host fan- out for cache selv er ude af stand til at v1."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The role deploys a single `registry:2` instance in pull-through proxy mode on its inventory group's host. Because the group typically holds exactly one host (the swarm manager), `DEPLOYMENT_MODE` resolves to `compose` for the role; multi-host fan-out for the cache itself is out of scope for v1."
msgstr "Den rolle, som en enkelt `registry:2` tilfælde i pull- through proxy mode på sin beholdning gruppens vært. Fordi gruppen typisk har præcis én vært (sværmbestyrer), `DEPLOYMENT_MODE` Beslutter `compose` for rollen; multi-host fan- out for cache selv er ude af stand til at v1."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The role deploys end-to-end on the project's reference distribution and is covered by **at least** a smoke-level Playwright spec, but neither the deploy nor the spec depth is considered production-grade."
msgstr "Denne rolle udmønter sig i slutningen af projektets referencedistribution og er dækket af **Mindst** et røgniveau Playwright spec, men hverken deployering eller spec dybde betragtes som produktion-kvalitet."

msgid "The role deploys the Semaphore server and a dedicated task runner and wires them into the platform via `SEMAPHORE_*` environment variables. The setup wizard is bypassed by seeding the initial admin from rendered secrets, so a fresh deploy lands directly on the Semaphore login page. When SSO is enabled, the Keycloak `administrator` is created at deploy time as an external Semaphore admin via `semaphore user add --admin --external`; the OIDC callback matches it by email and signs the operator in as a Semaphore admin. As the last step of every deploy the role converges the `Infinito.Nexus` project, whose stop and start templates let members of the `operator` role group pause and resume the applications of the host through [sys-svc-app-control](../sys-svc-app-control/)."
msgstr ""

msgid "The role deploys the Semaphore server and a dedicated task runner and wires them into the platform via ``SEMAPHORE_*`` environment variables. The setup wizard is bypassed by seeding the initial admin from rendered secrets, so a fresh deploy lands directly on the Semaphore login page. When SSO is enabled, the Keycloak ``administrator`` is created at deploy time as an external Semaphore admin via ``semaphore user add --admin --external``; the OIDC callback matches it by email and signs the operator in as a Semaphore admin. As the last step of every deploy the role converges the ``Infinito.Nexus`` project, whose stop and start templates let members of the ``operator`` role group pause and resume the applications of the host through `sys-svc-app-control <../sys-svc-app-control/>`__."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The role deploys the frontend and owns the templates and their tuning; the dev compose stack has no inventory to render them with and comes through here instead. Every value still has one home: the hosts and repositories come from the ``cache:`` declarations, the nginx tuning from the role's ``vars/main.yml``, and only the backend address differs, because the dev stack reaches Nexus over a compose network alias while the role reaches it by its configured container."
msgstr "Rollen udmønter frontend og ejer skabelonerne og deres tuning; dev komponere stak har ingen opgørelse til at gøre dem med og kommer igennem her i stedet. Hver værdi stadig har et hjem: værter og datalagre kommer fra ``cache:`` erklæringer, nginx tuning fra rolleens ``vars/main.yml``, og kun den bagende adresse adskiller sig, fordi dev stak når Nexus over en komponere netværk alias, mens rollen når det ved sin konfigurerede container."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The role deploys two containers on its inventory group's host: the repository manager and its nginx frontend. Both run in compose mode on the manager, like the sibling [svc-registry-cache](../svc-registry-cache/README.md)."
msgstr "Rollen anvender to containere på sin lagergruppes vært: lagerforvalteren og dens nginx frontend. Begge kører i komposition tilstand på manager, ligesom søskende [svc-registry-cache](../svc-registry-cache/README.md)."

