# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The search panel of the default source never lists a result: a query logs `Connecting to 'https://d1bplzhgyq-dsn.algolia.net/1/indexes/*/queries' violates the following Content Security Policy directive: \"connect-src 'self' https://cdn.<domain>\"` and the list stays empty (measured on the compose stack). Cause: the theme queries the Algolia index of the upstream site from the browser and `meta/csp.yml` declares no `connect-src` entry; an allowed request would return links into upstream's own pages. Options: whitelist the Algolia host under `connect-src` and accept upstream's index; or leave the request blocked and remove the search controls from the build."
msgstr "Søgepanelet for standardkilden viser aldrig et resultat: en forespørgsel logger `Connecting to 'https://d1bplzhgyq-dsn.algolia.net/1/indexes/*/queries' violates the following Content Security Policy directive: \"connect-src 'self' https://cdn.<domain>\"` og listen forbliver tom (målt på komponentstakken). Årsag: temaet spørger Algolia indeks af opstrøms site fra browseren og `meta/csp.yml` erklærer nej `connect-src` entry; en tilladt anmodning ville returnere links til opstrøms egne sider. Indstillinger: whitelist Algolia vært under `connect-src` og acceptere opstrøms indeks; eller efterlade anmodningen blokeret og fjerne søgekontrollen fra bygningen."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The section titles are the classification vocabulary itself, and each role that ships a `meta/mcp.yml` is filed under the value that file declares. The authoritative disposition of a deployed surface is that file; this list is the record of the review, including the roles that deliberately carry no surface."
msgstr "Sektionens titler er selve klassifikationsordforrådet, og hver rolle, der sender en `meta/mcp.yml` arkiveres under den værdi, som filen erklærer. Den autoritative disposition af en anvendt overflade er denne fil; denne liste er record af revisionen, herunder de roller, der bevidst bærer ingen overflade."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The security policies enforced on this repository are documented here:"
msgstr "Sikkerhedspolitikken på dette arkiv er dokumenteret her:"

msgid "The seeder starts every seeder script once per ``services.seeder.interval_seconds``. Each standalone seeder is capped by ``services.seeder.timeout_seconds`` (``SEED_TIMEOUT`` upstream), so one hung feed cannot block the ones after it. Seeded data lives in the ``cache_data`` volume, which survives container recreation and is excluded from the platform backup, because the seeder rebuilds it."
msgstr ""

msgid "The seeder starts every seeder script once per `services.seeder.interval_seconds`. Each standalone seeder is capped by `services.seeder.timeout_seconds` (`SEED_TIMEOUT` upstream), so one hung feed cannot block the ones after it. Seeded data lives in the `cache_data` volume, which survives container recreation and is excluded from the platform backup, because the seeder rebuilds it."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The selected deploy modes this row can actually run in. Never empty for a row the query returned -- the filter kept it precisely because at least one selected mode claims it."
msgstr "De valgte implementeringstilstande denne række kan faktisk køre i. Aldrig tom for en række forespørgslen returneres -- filteret holdt det præcist fordi mindst én valgt tilstand hævder det."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The selection and retry logic is implemented in   `scripts/install/ansible.sh`."
msgstr "Udvælgelsen og prøve logik er gennemført i `scripts/install/ansible.sh`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The selection tokens that reproduce exactly what did not pass."
msgstr "De valg tokens, der reproducere præcis, hvad der ikke bestået."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The selections of the last finished deploy run on the branch that are not green. `cli.administration.deploy.ci.selections.failed_selections` reads them straight out of the job titles, so each candidate arrives with the variant, mode and onion state it failed in."
msgstr "Udvælgelsen af den sidste færdige indsats køre på gren, der ikke er grøn. `cli.administration.deploy.ci.selections.failed_selections` læser dem lige ud af jobtitler, så hver kandidat ankommer med variant, mode og løg stat det mislykkedes i."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The sequenced flow lives in [`routine/`](routine/), the naming SPOT in `utils/topology/`, shared helpers in `utils/`, and the cluster declaration (image, containers, network, DNS play) in `compose/swarm/` + `compose/swarm/compose.yml`."
msgstr "Den sekvenserede strøm lever i [`routine/`](routine/), navngivning SPOT i `utils/topology/`, fælles hjælpere i `utils/`, og klyngeerklæringen (billede, containere, netværk, DNS-spil) til `compose/swarm/` + `compose/swarm/compose.yml`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The served upstream version moves with every deploy and every role sync: `services.littlejs.ref` in `meta/services.yml` is `main`, and the checkout updates to the head of that branch each run (served during the design pass: commit `8f863c14d114e984a59f42c6ef4b98093581f677`, past the newest tag `v1.25.0`). The role stylesheet maps the thirteen variables of upstream's `examples/style.css`, so an upstream change of that file can undo the mapping without any change in this repository. Options: pin `ref` to a tag such as `v1.25.0`; or pin it to a commit and let the version updater move it."
msgstr "Den serverede opstrømsversion bevæger sig med hver implementering og hver rolle synkronisering: `services.littlejs.ref` til `meta/services.yml` er `main`, og checkout opdateringer til lederen af denne gren hver køre (serveret under designpasset: commit `8f863c14d114e984a59f42c6ef4b98093581f677`, forbi det nyeste mærke `v1.25.0`). Rollestylesheet kortlægger de tretten variabler i opstrøms `examples/style.css`, så en opstrømsændring af denne fil kan fortryde kortlægningen uden nogen ændring i dette arkiv. Indstillinger: pin `ref` til et mærke som `v1.25.0`; eller fastgør det til en forpligtelse og lad versionen updater flytte det."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The server answers with its input, lightly reworded, often enough that the result keeps every span and every markup character while still being English. Comparing scripts catches it wherever the target does not use the Latin one; for a Latin-script target it would need a language detector."
msgstr "Serveren svarer med sit input, let omformuleret, ofte nok til at resultatet holder hver span og hver markup karakter, mens stadig er engelsk. Sammenligning scripts fanger det overalt, hvor målet ikke bruger den latinske; for en latin- script mål det ville have brug for en sprogdetektor."

msgid "The server authenticates against a users file. The role renders it from the directory users whose password is pinned in the inventory (``lookup('users_non_reserved', pinned_only=true)``), so they sign in with their platform username and that password. Bots and accounts with a host login are left out: the host login’s password is the server’s become password and must not reach a third-party form, so the ``administrator`` account renders through a personal account. Passwords are stored as scrypt hashes in the format of the upstream ``passwd.mjs``; the per-user salt is derived from ``secrets.credentials.users_salt_key``, so a rerun writes the same file and only a changed password recreates the container."
msgstr ""

msgid "The server authenticates against a users file. The role renders it from the directory users whose password is pinned in the inventory (`lookup('users_non_reserved', pinned_only=true)`), so they sign in with their platform username and that password. Bots and accounts with a host login are left out: the host login's password is the server's become password and must not reach a third-party form, so the `administrator` account renders through a personal account. Passwords are stored as scrypt hashes in the format of the upstream `passwd.mjs`; the per-user salt is derived from `secrets.credentials.users_salt_key`, so a rerun writes the same file and only a changed password recreates the container."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The server needs an active browser tab and plugin connection, and can execute powerful design-context operations."
msgstr "Serveren har brug for en aktiv browser fane og plugin forbindelse, og kan udføre kraftfulde design- kontekst operationer."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The server starts with a token from the deployment's credential store, binds to the container network and publishes no port. Cross-site request checking is off and any origin is accepted, because the caller is a service on the same network that presents the token rather than a browser carrying a cookie."
msgstr "Serveren starter med en token fra deployeringens kreditforretning, binder sig til containernetværket og udgiver ingen port. Cross-site anmodning kontrol er slukket og enhver oprindelse er accepteret, fordi opkalderen er en tjeneste på samme netværk, der præsenterer token snarere end en browser med en cookie."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The server starts with a token from the deployment’s credential store, binds to the container network and publishes no port. Cross-site request checking is off and any origin is accepted, because the caller is a service on the same network that presents the token rather than a browser carrying a cookie."
msgstr "Serveren starter med en token fra deployeringens kreditforretning, binder sig til containernetværket og udgiver ingen port. Cross-site anmodning kontrol er slukket og enhver oprindelse er accepteret, fordi opkalderen er en tjeneste på samme netværk, der præsenterer token snarere end en browser med en cookie."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The server's own thread count follows the CPUs its container may use, which a deploy decides; only the client side is free to vary per run. This sweeps it against real catalog entries and records the winner for the env builder, so a tuned host keeps its numbers across every `make dotenv`."
msgstr "Serverens egen trådtælling følger CPU 'erne dens beholder kan bruge, som en implementering beslutter; kun klientsiden er fri til at variere per løb. Dette sweeps det mod rigtige katalog poster og registrerer vinderen for env builder, så en tunet vært holder sine numre på tværs af hver `make dotenv`."

msgid "The service block that pulls the provider into the inventory and makes the service loader preload it."
msgstr ""

msgid "The service holds no Keycloak administration rights and no service account. It grants a confirmed request with the approving administrator's own token, and Keycloak's fine-grained admin permissions (v2) are the only authority on who may grant which group; the deploy generates those permissions from every role's `meta/rbac.yml`."
msgstr ""

msgid "The service is rendered only when `services.bridge.enabled` is true, which defaults to `web-app-mobilizon` and `web-app-bluesky` both being in `group_names`. Without either partner the compose file carries no `bridge` service and the deploy runs without it."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The service registry (service key -> provider role) stays built from the full rendered base set so provider discovery is unaffected by the active variants; only the dep-walk sees the variant configs (with the swarm force-shared DB view applied on top)."
msgstr "Serviceregistret (servicenøgle - > leverandørens rolle) ophold bygget fra det fuldt leverede base sæt, så udbyder opdagelse er upåvirket af de aktive varianter; kun dep- walk ser variant config (med den sværmfulde kraft-delte DB visning anvendes på toppen)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The service runs as a lightweight Node.js app backed by PostgreSQL."
msgstr "Tjenesten kører som en letvægts Node.js app bakkes op af PostgreSQL."

msgid "The service sits behind the oauth2-proxy gate of [web-app-keycloak](../web-app-keycloak/) without a group requirement. Its gate sets `any_email`, so it admits a realm user of any email domain. It reads the requester only from the gate's headers, never from the form."
msgstr ""

msgid "The service sits behind the oauth2-proxy gate of `web-app-keycloak <../web-app-keycloak/>`__ without a group requirement. Its gate sets ``any_email``, so it admits a realm user of any email domain. It reads the requester only from the gate’s headers, never from the form."
msgstr ""

msgid "The sets dnsmasq fills (`tor_dns_*`, `direct_dns_*`) expire after `TOR_EGRESS_NFTSET_TIMEOUT` (1h). dnsmasq caps its cache at `max-cache-ttl=300`, so a client that keeps resolving refreshes its entry, and the deploy sends dnsmasq `SIGHUP` after every firewall reload so the next answers refill the emptied sets."
msgstr ""

# "failIfUnavailable": true }`. Dette forhindrer en farlig fejl-
# sikkerhedstilstand: hvis OS- niveau sandkasse motor (F.eks. `bwrap` på Linux
# `sandbox-exec` på macOS) mangler eller fungerer ikke Claude Code ville
# ellers stille falde tilbage til ingen sandboksning, mens
# `autoAllowBashIfSandboxed` fortsætter med at auto- godkende kommandoer som
# om de var begrænset. Med `failIfUnavailable: true`, Claude Code nægter at gå
# videre i denne situation, tvinger operatøren til at installere den manglende
# motor eller udtrykkeligt nedgradere politikken, før nogen kommando kører.
# Bidragydere på systemer uden en fungerende sandkasse bagenden SKAL
# installere den relevante binære snarere end at svække dette flag lokalt.
# translated-by: libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "The settings file additionally sets `\"sandbox\": { \"failIfUnavailable\": true }`. This prevents a dangerous false-security state: if the OS-level sandbox backend (e.g. `bwrap` on Linux, `sandbox-exec` on macOS) is missing or non-functional, Claude Code would otherwise silently fall back to no sandboxing while `autoAllowBashIfSandboxed` continues to auto-approve commands as if they were confined. With `failIfUnavailable: true`, Claude Code refuses to proceed in that situation, forcing the operator to install the missing backend or explicitly downgrade the policy before any command runs. Contributors on systems without a working sandbox backend MUST install the appropriate binary rather than weakening this flag locally."
msgstr "Indstillingsfilen indstiller desuden `\"sandbox\": { \"failIfUnavailable\": true }`. Dette forhindrer en farlig fejl- sikkerhedstilstand: hvis OS- niveau sandkasse motor (F.eks. `bwrap` på Linux `sandbox-exec` på macOS) mangler eller fungerer ikke Claude Code ville ellers stille falde tilbage til ingen sandboksning, mens `autoAllowBashIfSandboxed` fortsætter med at auto- godkende kommandoer som om de var begrænset. Med `failIfUnavailable: true`, Claude Code nægter at gå videre i denne situation, tvinger operatøren til at installere den manglende motor eller udtrykkeligt nedgradere politikken, før nogen kommando kører. Bidragydere på systemer uden en fungerende sandkasse bagenden SKAL installere den relevante binære snarere end at svække dette flag lokalt."

msgid "The setup tasks handle the full first-deploy bootstrap automatically. Steps 1 to 3 run on every deploy, with or without SSO; step 4 runs only when ``services.sso.enabled`` is ``true``:"
msgstr ""

msgid "The setup tasks handle the full first-deploy bootstrap automatically. Steps 1 to 3 run on every deploy, with or without SSO; step 4 runs only when `services.sso.enabled` is `true`:"
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The shape each key must have is declared per role rather than here, in [roles/svc-ai-litellm/meta/secrets.yml](../../../../../roles/svc-ai-litellm/meta/secrets.yml) with a `type:` and a `regex:`. The pattern rejects a truncated or whitespace-carrying paste and deliberately accepts any vendor prefix, so a provider changing its issuance format cannot turn a valid key into a failed inventory run."
msgstr "Den form, hver nøgle skal have, er angivet pr. rolle snarere end her, i [roles/svc-ai-litellm/meta/secrets.yml](../../../../../roles/svc-ai-litellm/meta/secrets.yml) med `type:` og a `regex:`. Mønsteret afviser en trunkeret eller whitespace- carriing pasta og bevidst accepterer enhver leverandør præfiks, så en udbyder ændre sin udstedelse format kan ikke vende en gyldig nøgle til en mislykket opgørelse køre."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The shape every consumer renders from: the ansible lookups, which then apply the inventory, and the dev stack, which does not."
msgstr "Formen hver forbruger giver fra: de ansible opslag, som derefter anvender fortegnelsen, og dev stak, som ikke gør."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The shape mirrors the schema tree: nested keys stay nested. The literal string is preserved verbatim, with no rendering and no validation. Leaves WITHOUT ``default:`` are intentionally absent so the inventory's apply_schema-generated values win the merge."
msgstr "Formen afspejler skema træ: indlejrede nøgler bo indlejret. Den bogstavelige streng er bevaret ordret, uden rendering og ingen validering. Blade UDEN ``default:`` er bevidst fraværende, så opgørelsen er apply_schema-genererede værdier vinder sammenfletningen."

msgid "The shared ``administrator`` persona journey is opted out via ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED`` in ``templates/playwright.env.j2``. Flowise has no in-app OIDC adapter: SSO is an oauth2-proxy sidecar (``services.sso.flavor: oauth2``), and behind that gate Flowise still presents its own sign-in form for its single instance account ``flowise-api-bot``, which ``tasks/utils/owner.yml`` registers. The Keycloak administrator credential the persona types is not that account’s, so the journey cannot reach an authenticated Flowise surface; the OIDC gate itself is covered by ``files/playwright/test-oidc-login.js``."
msgstr ""

# hjælpere er erklæret blokeret i `templates/playwright.env.j2
# <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__. Nextcloud præsenterer tre forskellige
# login-overflader afhængigt af varianten (indfødt ``oidc_login``,
# ``sociallogin``), den indfødte administrator autentificerer med role- lokale
# ``credentials.administrator_password`` (Bifald) Keycloak hemmelighed, og
# ``#firstrunwizard`` modal opsnapper brugermenuen klik på den generiske
# logout afhænger af. Begge personas er derfor drevet af rollens egne login
# specs - ``test-login-admin-native.js``, ``test-login-admin-oidc.js``,
# ``test-login-biber-oidc.js`` og ``test-login-biber-ldap.js`` under
# ``files/playwright/`` - som bærer smagen switch, modale afskedigelse og
# login igen den delte hjælper mangler.
msgid "The shared ``biber`` and ``administrator`` persona helpers are declared blocked in `templates/playwright.env.j2 <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__. Nextcloud presents three different login surfaces depending on the variant (native, ``oidc_login``, ``sociallogin``), the native administrator authenticates with the role-local ``credentials.administrator_password`` rather than the Keycloak secret, and the ``#firstrunwizard`` modal intercepts the user-menu click the generic logout depends on. Both personas are therefore driven by the role’s own login specs — ``test-login-admin-native.js``, ``test-login-admin-oidc.js``, ``test-login-biber-oidc.js`` and ``test-login-biber-ldap.js`` under ``files/playwright/`` — which carry the flavor switch, the modal dismissal and the login retry the shared helper lacks."
msgstr ""

msgid "The shared ``biber`` and ``administrator`` persona helpers are declared blocked in `templates/playwright.env.j2 <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__. Odoo renders its SSO provider link only on ``/web/login`` inside the ``.o_login_auth`` container, not on the site root the persona helper starts from, and it exposes no in-app logout control — signing out means navigating to ``/web/session/logout``. The full Keycloak round trip for both users is covered by the role’s own ``odoo: admin sso login, verify ui, logout`` and ``odoo: biber sso login, verify ui, logout`` scenarios in `files/playwright/playwright.spec.js <./files/playwright/playwright.spec.js>`__; the second joins ``biber`` to the ``user`` role group first, because a Keycloak user without an Odoo role is refused. `files/playwright/test-rbac.js <./files/playwright/test-rbac.js>`__ covers every role and the profile mapping."
msgstr ""

# hjælpere er erklæret blokeret i `templates/playwright.env.j2
# <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__. OpenCloud Web svar Playwright 's
# hovedløse Chromium bruger agent med en "browser ikke understøttet" splash
# medmindre ``forceAllowOldBrowser`` er sået i ``localStorage`` før den første
# navigation, og dens OIDC callback løber igennem OpenCloudegne
# ``/oidc-callback`` → ``/web-oidc-callback`` ruter i stedet for
# oauth2-Proxymønster den delte hjælper registrerer. Begge personer " Keycloak
# rundtur er dækket af `files/playwright/test-sso-login.js
# <./files/playwright/test-sso-login.js>`__, som gør, at priming i
# `files/playwright/\_shared.js <./files/playwright/_shared.js>`__.
# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The shared ``biber`` and ``administrator`` persona helpers are declared blocked in `templates/playwright.env.j2 <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__. OpenCloud Web answers Playwright’s headless Chromium user agent with a “browser not supported” splash unless ``forceAllowOldBrowser`` is seeded into ``localStorage`` before the first navigation, and its OIDC callback runs through OpenCloud’s own ``/oidc-callback`` → ``/web-oidc-callback`` routes instead of the oauth2-proxy pattern the shared helper detects. Both personas’ Keycloak round trip is covered by `files/playwright/test-sso-login.js <./files/playwright/test-sso-login.js>`__, which does that priming in `files/playwright/\\_shared.js <./files/playwright/_shared.js>`__."
msgstr "Den delte ``biber`` og ``administrator`` persona hjælpere er erklæret blokeret i `templates/playwright.env.j2 <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__. OpenCloud Web svar Playwright 's hovedløse Chromium bruger agent med en \"browser ikke understøttet\" splash medmindre ``forceAllowOldBrowser`` er sået i ``localStorage`` før den første navigation, og dens OIDC callback løber igennem OpenCloudegne ``/oidc-callback`` → ``/web-oidc-callback`` ruter i stedet for oauth2-Proxymønster den delte hjælper registrerer. Begge personer \" Keycloak rundtur er dækket af `files/playwright/test-sso-login.js <./files/playwright/test-sso-login.js>`__, som gør, at priming i `files/playwright/\\_shared.js <./files/playwright/_shared.js>`__."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The shared ``biber`` and ``administrator`` persona helpers are declared blocked in `templates/playwright.env.j2 <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__. Pixelfed’s login id is the account e-mail rather than the Keycloak username, and the artisan-bootstrapped administrator name is reserved, so pixelfed’s first-time OIDC registration cannot mint it either. ``biber`` additionally needs his Keycloak e-mail rewritten to a resolvable domain through the Keycloak admin API before the first OIDC login, because pixelfed’s ``dns,spoof`` validator rejects ``.example`` addresses. Both setups live in `files/playwright/\\_shared.js <./files/playwright/_shared.js>`__ and drive the dedicated login specs in ``files/playwright/``."
msgstr "Den delte ``biber`` og ``administrator`` persona hjælpere er erklæret blokeret i `templates/playwright.env.j2 <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__. Pixeleds login id er kontoen e-mail snarere end den Keycloak brugernavn, og den håndlavede-bootstrapped administrator navn er reserveret, så pixelfed første gang OIDC registrering kan ikke mint det enten. ``biber`` desuden har brug for hans Keycloak e-mail omskrevet til et område, der kan løses gennem Keycloak admin API før det første OIDC login, fordi pixelfed 's ``dns,spoof`` Validator afviser ``.example`` adresser. Begge opsætninger bor i `files/playwright/\\_shared.js <./files/playwright/_shared.js>`__ og køre de dedikerede login specs i ``files/playwright/``."

# hjælpere er erklæret blokeret i `templates/playwright.env.j2
# <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__. OpenTalk frontend er en public- client
# OIDC single- page app - containeren env bærer intet andet end udsteder og
# klient id, der er ingen server- side session og ingen HTML login form - så
# rollen driver det med sin egen redirect- racing hjælper keyed på ``LOGIN_*``
# / ``BIBER_*`` I stedet for ``ADMIN_*`` par den delte hjælper forventer, og
# browser- side session forlader kontrakten in-app logout ben uden et mål.
# Begge personer " Keycloak → dashboard kæde er dækket af
# `files/playwright/test-sso-login.js
# <./files/playwright/test-sso-login.js>`__.
# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The shared ``biber`` and ``administrator`` persona helpers are declared blocked in `templates/playwright.env.j2 <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__. The OpenTalk frontend is a public-client OIDC single-page app — the container env carries nothing but the issuer and the client id, there is no server-side session and no HTML login form — so the role drives it with its own redirect-racing helper keyed on ``LOGIN_*`` / ``BIBER_*`` instead of the ``ADMIN_*`` pair the shared helper expects, and the browser-side session leaves the contract’s in-app logout leg without a target. Both personas’ Keycloak → dashboard chain is covered by `files/playwright/test-sso-login.js <./files/playwright/test-sso-login.js>`__."
msgstr "Den delte ``biber`` og ``administrator`` persona hjælpere er erklæret blokeret i `templates/playwright.env.j2 <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__. OpenTalk frontend er en public- client OIDC single- page app - containeren env bærer intet andet end udsteder og klient id, der er ingen server- side session og ingen HTML login form - så rollen driver det med sin egen redirect- racing hjælper keyed på ``LOGIN_*`` / ``BIBER_*`` I stedet for ``ADMIN_*`` par den delte hjælper forventer, og browser- side session forlader kontrakten in-app logout ben uden et mål. Begge personer \" Keycloak → dashboard kæde er dækket af `files/playwright/test-sso-login.js <./files/playwright/test-sso-login.js>`__."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The shared ``biber`` and ``administrator`` persona helpers are declared blocked in `templates/playwright.env.j2 <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__. The role provisions no pretix account at all — `tasks/main.yml <./tasks/main.yml>`__ only deploys the stack — while pretix’s native auth backend authenticates a pretix ``User`` row that is created by the interactive first-run setup. The ``pretix-oidc`` backend added on top lives on pretix’s ``/control`` login page, whereas the role’s base URL serves the public ticket shop that the baseline scenarios in `files/playwright/playwright.spec.js <./files/playwright/playwright.spec.js>`__ assert. Seeding a backend user is the path back to a runnable persona journey."
msgstr "Den delte ``biber`` og ``administrator`` persona hjælpere er erklæret blokeret i `templates/playwright.env.j2 <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__. Den rolle bestemmelser ingen pretix konto overhovedet - `tasks/main.yml <./tasks/main.yml>`__ kun implementerer stakken - mens Pretix 's indfødte auth-motor godkender en pretix ``User`` række, der er skabt af den interaktive first-run setup. Den ``pretix-oidc`` backend tilføjet på øverste liv på pretix 's ``/control`` login side, mens rollens base URL tjener den offentlige billet shop, at baseline scenarier i `files/playwright/playwright.spec.js <./files/playwright/playwright.spec.js>`__ - Det er sandt. Seeding en backend bruger er stien tilbage til en løbende persona rejse."

# rejser er valgt ud via ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED`` /
# ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED`` til ``templates/playwright.env.j2``.
# Fiders SSO indgang er en totrins modal: header "Log ind" knappen åbner kun
# den udbyder dialog, og et andet klik på "Fortsæt med... SSO" udfører
# Keycloak omdirigerer, mens den delte hjælper klikker præcis én gang og
# aldrig når IdP. Begge rejser er dækket af denne rolles egen ``fider: admin
# sso login`` og ``fider: biber sso login as regular user`` scenarier i
# ``files/playwright/playwright.spec.js``; Opt- out bortfalder, når den delte
# hjælper lærer Fider's modal.
# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The shared ``biber`` and ``administrator`` persona journeys are opted out via ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED`` / ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED`` in ``templates/playwright.env.j2``. Fider’s SSO entry is a two-step modal: the header “Sign in” button only opens the provider dialog, and a second click on “Continue with … SSO” performs the Keycloak redirect, whereas the shared helper clicks exactly once and never reaches the IdP. Both journeys are covered end-to-end by this role’s own ``fider: admin sso login`` and ``fider: biber sso login as regular user`` scenarios in ``files/playwright/playwright.spec.js``; the opt-out lapses once the shared helper learns Fider’s modal."
msgstr "Den delte ``biber`` og ``administrator`` persona rejser er valgt ud via ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED`` / ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED`` til ``templates/playwright.env.j2``. Fiders SSO indgang er en totrins modal: header \"Log ind\" knappen åbner kun den udbyder dialog, og et andet klik på \"Fortsæt med... SSO\" udfører Keycloak omdirigerer, mens den delte hjælper klikker præcis én gang og aldrig når IdP. Begge rejser er dækket af denne rolles egen ``fider: admin sso login`` og ``fider: biber sso login as regular user`` scenarier i ``files/playwright/playwright.spec.js``; Opt- out bortfalder, når den delte hjælper lærer Fider's modal."

# translated-by: libretranslate
#, no-python-format, python-brace-format
msgid "The shared ``biber`` and ``administrator`` persona journeys are opted out via ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED`` / ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED`` in ``templates/playwright.env.j2``. Outside the OIDC variant, ``templates/casc.yaml.j2`` selects the ``ldap`` or ``local`` security realm and Jenkins’ only login surface is its own Java-realm form, whose fields are named ``j_username`` / ``j_password`` (pinned by the LDAP scenario in ``files/playwright/playwright.spec.js``) — names the shared native-login probe does not match, so the persona never authenticates. The flag is currently unconditional; narrowing it to ``{% if not JENKINS_OIDC_ENABLED %}`` once the OIDC persona journey has been verified end-to-end is the path back."
msgstr "Den delte ``biber`` og ``administrator`` persona rejser er valgt ud via ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED`` / ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED`` til ``templates/playwright.env.j2``. Uden for OIDC variant, ``templates/casc.yaml.j2`` vælger ``ldap`` eller ``local`` sikkerhedsområde og Jenkins'Kun login overflade er sin egen Java-rige form, hvis felter er navngivet ``j_username`` / ``j_password`` (som følge af LDAP-scenariet i ``files/playwright/playwright.spec.js``) - navngiver den delte indfødte-login sonde ikke matcher, så persona aldrig autentificerer. Flaget er i øjeblikket betingelsesløst; indsnævring af det til ``{% if not JENKINS_OIDC_ENABLED %}`` Når OIDC persona rejse er blevet verificeret end-to-end er stien tilbage."

msgid "The shared ``biber`` and ``administrator`` persona journeys are opted out via ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED`` / ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED`` in ``templates/playwright.env.j2``. The site front page renders no logout control: Joomla’s site template places no login module, and the only rendered Log out button sits on the com_users login view, so the persona’s mandatory in-app logout click on the front page has no target and navigating a logout URL directly is forbidden by the contract. The OIDC handshake itself, the Keycloak logout from the com_users Log out button, the LDAP variant and the ``/administrator?fallback=local`` hatch are covered by ``files/playwright/test-oidc-login.js``, ``test-sso-logout.js``, ``test-ldap-login.js`` and ``test-oidc-fallback.js``."
msgstr ""

msgid "The shared ``biber`` and ``administrator`` persona journeys are opted out via ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED`` / ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED`` in ``templates/playwright.env.j2``. ``biber`` holds no FusionDirectory role, so the oauth2-proxy denies it. ```files/playwright/test-rbac.js`` <./files/playwright/test-rbac.js>`__ asserts that denial and adds ``biber`` to each role group in turn to assert the rights of the matching ACL role. The shared admin flow has not been verified against the header login. ```files/playwright/test-design.js`` <./files/playwright/test-design.js>`__ asserts the administrator’s sign-in and rights in both variants, and ```files/playwright/playwright.spec.js`` <./files/playwright/playwright.spec.js>`__ asserts that the Keycloak sign-in lands in FusionDirectory without a second login form."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The shared ``biber`` and ``administrator`` persona journeys are opted out via ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED`` / ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED`` in ``templates/playwright.env.j2``. web-app-hugo serves a statically built site: ``services.sso`` is hard-disabled in ``meta/services.yml``, the container is a Hugo build baked into nginx (``templates/compose.yml.j2``), and the Playwright env file renders no ``ADMIN_*`` / ``BIBER_*`` credentials. There is no session, no admin surface and no logout control to drive, so the ``guest`` persona plus the reachability, CSP and rendered-HTML assertions are the complete contract for this role."
msgstr "Den delte ``biber`` og ``administrator`` persona rejser er valgt ud via ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED`` / ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED`` til ``templates/playwright.env.j2``. web-app-hugo betjener et statisk bygget sted: ``services.sso`` er hard- deaktiveret i ``meta/services.yml``, containeren er en Hugo bygge bagt til nginx (``templates/compose.yml.j2``), og Playwright env fil gør ingen ``ADMIN_*`` / ``BIBER_*`` legitimation. Der er ingen session, ingen admin overflade og ingen logout kontrol til at køre, så ``guest`` persona plus adgang, CSP og rendered- HTML påstande er den komplette kontrakt for denne rolle."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The shared ``biber`` persona journey is opted out via ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED`` in ``templates/playwright.env.j2``. A Jellyfin account binds to exactly one authentication provider, so biber’s login is owned by the per-addon specs that know which provider is live: ``files/playwright/addons/sso-authentication.spec.js`` for OIDC and ``addons/ldap-authentication.spec.js`` for the LDAP-only matrix variant. The generic persona cannot pick between them and would duplicate or contradict that coverage; ``playwright.spec.js`` keeps the ``guest`` scenario and the native administrator login."
msgstr "Den delte ``biber`` persona rejse er valgt ud via ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED`` til ``templates/playwright.env.j2``. A Jellyfin konto binder sig til præcis én autentificering udbyder, så bibers login er ejet af per- addon specs, der ved, hvilken udbyder er live: ``files/playwright/addons/sso-authentication.spec.js`` for OIDC og ``addons/ldap-authentication.spec.js`` for LDAP-matrixvarianten. Den generiske persona kan ikke vælge mellem dem og ville duplikere eller modsige denne dækning; ``playwright.spec.js`` holder ``guest`` scenario og den indfødte administrator login."

msgid "The shared `administrator` persona journey is opted out via `PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED` in `templates/playwright.env.j2`. Flowise has no in-app OIDC adapter: SSO is an oauth2-proxy sidecar (`services.sso.flavor: oauth2`), and behind that gate Flowise still presents its own sign-in form for its single instance account `flowise-api-bot`, which `tasks/utils/owner.yml` registers. The Keycloak administrator credential the persona types is not that account's, so the journey cannot reach an authenticated Flowise surface; the OIDC gate itself is covered by `files/playwright/test-oidc-login.js`."
msgstr ""

# er erklæret blokeret i
# [templates/playwright.env.j2](./templates/playwright.env.j2). Nextcloud
# præsenterer tre forskellige login-overflader afhængigt af varianten (indfødt
# `oidc_login`, `sociallogin`), den indfødte administrator autentificerer med
# role- lokale `credentials.administrator_password` (Bifald) Keycloak
# hemmelighed, og `#firstrunwizard` modal opsnapper brugermenuen klik på den
# generiske logout afhænger af. Begge personas er derfor drevet af rollens
# egne login specs - `test-login-admin-native.js`, `test-login-admin-oidc.js`,
# `test-login-biber-oidc.js` og `test-login-biber-ldap.js` under
# `files/playwright/` - som bærer smagen switch, modale afskedigelse og login
# igen den delte hjælper mangler.
msgid "The shared `biber` and `administrator` persona helpers are declared blocked in [templates/playwright.env.j2](./templates/playwright.env.j2). Nextcloud presents three different login surfaces depending on the variant (native, `oidc_login`, `sociallogin`), the native administrator authenticates with the role-local `credentials.administrator_password` rather than the Keycloak secret, and the `#firstrunwizard` modal intercepts the user-menu click the generic logout depends on. Both personas are therefore driven by the role's own login specs — `test-login-admin-native.js`, `test-login-admin-oidc.js`, `test-login-biber-oidc.js` and `test-login-biber-ldap.js` under `files/playwright/` — which carry the flavor switch, the modal dismissal and the login retry the shared helper lacks."
msgstr ""

msgid "The shared `biber` and `administrator` persona helpers are declared blocked in [templates/playwright.env.j2](./templates/playwright.env.j2). Odoo renders its SSO provider link only on `/web/login` inside the `.o_login_auth` container, not on the site root the persona helper starts from, and it exposes no in-app logout control — signing out means navigating to `/web/session/logout`. The full Keycloak round trip for both users is covered by the role's own `odoo: admin sso login, verify ui, logout` and `odoo: biber sso login, verify ui, logout` scenarios in [files/playwright/playwright.spec.js](./files/playwright/playwright.spec.js); the second joins `biber` to the `user` role group first, because a Keycloak user without an Odoo role is refused. [files/playwright/test-rbac.js](./files/playwright/test-rbac.js) covers every role and the profile mapping."
msgstr ""

# er erklæret blokeret i
# [templates/playwright.env.j2](./templates/playwright.env.j2). OpenCloud Web
# svar Playwright 's hovedløse Chromium bruger agent med en "browser ikke
# understøttet" splash medmindre `forceAllowOldBrowser` er sået i
# `localStorage` før den første navigation, og dens OIDC callback løber
# igennem OpenCloudegne `/oidc-callback` → `/web-oidc-callback` ruter i stedet
# for oauth2-Proxymønster den delte hjælper registrerer. Begge personer "
# Keycloak rundtur er dækket af
# [files/playwright/test-sso-login.js](./files/playwright/test-sso-login.js),
# som gør, at priming i
# [files/playwright/_shared.js](./files/playwright/_shared.js).
# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The shared `biber` and `administrator` persona helpers are declared blocked in [templates/playwright.env.j2](./templates/playwright.env.j2). OpenCloud Web answers Playwright's headless Chromium user agent with a \"browser not supported\" splash unless `forceAllowOldBrowser` is seeded into `localStorage` before the first navigation, and its OIDC callback runs through OpenCloud's own `/oidc-callback` → `/web-oidc-callback` routes instead of the oauth2-proxy pattern the shared helper detects. Both personas' Keycloak round trip is covered by [files/playwright/test-sso-login.js](./files/playwright/test-sso-login.js), which does that priming in [files/playwright/_shared.js](./files/playwright/_shared.js)."
msgstr "Den delte `biber` og `administrator` persona hjælpere er erklæret blokeret i [templates/playwright.env.j2](./templates/playwright.env.j2). OpenCloud Web svar Playwright 's hovedløse Chromium bruger agent med en \"browser ikke understøttet\" splash medmindre `forceAllowOldBrowser` er sået i `localStorage` før den første navigation, og dens OIDC callback løber igennem OpenCloudegne `/oidc-callback` → `/web-oidc-callback` ruter i stedet for oauth2-Proxymønster den delte hjælper registrerer. Begge personer \" Keycloak rundtur er dækket af [files/playwright/test-sso-login.js](./files/playwright/test-sso-login.js), som gør, at priming i [files/playwright/_shared.js](./files/playwright/_shared.js)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The shared `biber` and `administrator` persona helpers are declared blocked in [templates/playwright.env.j2](./templates/playwright.env.j2). Pixelfed's login id is the account e-mail rather than the Keycloak username, and the artisan-bootstrapped administrator name is reserved, so pixelfed's first-time OIDC registration cannot mint it either. `biber` additionally needs his Keycloak e-mail rewritten to a resolvable domain through the Keycloak admin API before the first OIDC login, because pixelfed's `dns,spoof` validator rejects `.example` addresses. Both setups live in [files/playwright/_shared.js](./files/playwright/_shared.js) and drive the dedicated login specs in `files/playwright/`."
msgstr "Den delte `biber` og `administrator` persona hjælpere er erklæret blokeret i [templates/playwright.env.j2](./templates/playwright.env.j2). Pixeleds login id er kontoen e-mail snarere end den Keycloak brugernavn, og den håndlavede-bootstrapped administrator navn er reserveret, så pixelfed første gang OIDC registrering kan ikke mint det enten. `biber` desuden har brug for hans Keycloak e-mail omskrevet til et område, der kan løses gennem Keycloak admin API før det første OIDC login, fordi pixelfed 's `dns,spoof` Validator afviser `.example` adresser. Begge opsætninger bor i [files/playwright/_shared.js](./files/playwright/_shared.js) og køre de dedikerede login specs i `files/playwright/`."

# er erklæret blokeret i
# [templates/playwright.env.j2](./templates/playwright.env.j2). OpenTalk
# frontend er en public- client OIDC single- page app - containeren env bærer
# intet andet end udsteder og klient id, der er ingen server- side session og
# ingen HTML login form - så rollen driver det med sin egen redirect- racing
# hjælper keyed på `LOGIN_*` / `BIBER_*` I stedet for `ADMIN_*` par den delte
