# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "This role deploys Baserow using Docker Compose, integrating key components such as PostgreSQL for the database, Redis for caching, and NGINX for secure domain management and certificate handling. It is designed to offer a robust, scalable solution for running your own Baserow instance in a containerized environment."
msgstr "Denne rolle udspiller sig Baserow anvendelse Docker Compose, integration af nøglekomponenter såsom PostgreSQL for databasen Redis til caching og NGINX til sikker domæneforvaltning og certifikathåndtering. Det er designet til at tilbyde en robust, skalerbar løsning til at køre din egen Baserow eksempel i et containeriseret miljø."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "This role deploys Coturn via Docker Compose using the ``sys-stk-semi-stateless`` stack."
msgstr "Denne rolle udspiller sig Coturn via Docker Compose ved at bruge ``sys-stk-semi-stateless`` stack."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "This role deploys Coturn via Docker Compose using the `sys-stk-semi-stateless` stack.   It automatically configures:"
msgstr "Denne rolle udspiller sig Coturn via Docker Compose ved at bruge `sys-stk-semi-stateless` stack. Det automatisk sletter:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "This role deploys Discourse using Docker, automating tasks such as container orchestration, service configuration, and routine administrative operations. It integrates key components like Redis and PostgreSQL, sets up domain routing with NGINX, and ensures streamlined updates for a reliable forum experience."
msgstr "Denne rolle udspiller sig Discourse brug af Docker, automatisering opgaver såsom container orkestrering, service konfiguration, og rutinemæssige administrative operationer. Det integrerer nøglekomponenter som Redis og PostgreSQL, opretter domæneruting med NGINX og sikrer strømlinede opdateringer for en pålidelig forumoplevelse."

msgid "This role deploys ERPNext as an Infinito.Nexus web app using the upstream ``frappe/erpnext`` single-image multi-role pattern from `frappe_docker <https://github.com/frappe/frappe_docker>`__: one Docker image, different commands per container (backend gunicorn, frontend nginx, websocket socketio, scheduler, two queue workers, plus a one-shot configurator). MariaDB and Redis come from the central ``svc-db-mariadb`` and ``svc-db-redis`` providers — the three Frappe Redis logical roles (``cache``, ``queue``, ``socketio``) share one central Redis instance via DB-number split (0 / 1 / 2). Authentication uses Frappe’s built-in Social Login Key against the shared Keycloak OIDC client without an oauth2-proxy sidecar; LDAP federation and outbound SMTP via the mail server (`web-app-email <../web-app-email/>`__) are wired when their providers are present."
msgstr ""

msgid "This role deploys ERPNext as an Infinito.Nexus web app using the upstream `frappe/erpnext` single-image multi-role pattern from [frappe_docker](https://github.com/frappe/frappe_docker): one Docker image, different commands per container (backend gunicorn, frontend nginx, websocket socketio, scheduler, two queue workers, plus a one-shot configurator). MariaDB and Redis come from the central `svc-db-mariadb` and `svc-db-redis` providers — the three Frappe Redis logical roles (`cache`, `queue`, `socketio`) share one central Redis instance via DB-number split (0 / 1 / 2). Authentication uses Frappe's built-in Social Login Key against the shared Keycloak OIDC client without an oauth2-proxy sidecar; LDAP federation and outbound SMTP via the mail server ([web-app-email](../web-app-email/)) are wired when their providers are present."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "This role deploys Fider as part of the Infinito.Nexus stack using a single Docker Compose container backed by PostgreSQL. It configures SSO via Keycloak automatically on first deploy, optional email notifications via Mailu, and HTTPS via NGINX reverse proxy."
msgstr "Denne rolle udspiller sig Fider som en del af Infinito.Nexus stack ved hjælp af en enkelt Docker Compose beholder med PostgreSQLDet forklarer SSO via Keycloak automatisk på første implementering, valgfri e-mail-meddelelser via Mailu, og HTTPS via NGINX reverse proxy."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "This role deploys Friendica using Docker, managing the Friendica application container alongside a central MariaDB instance. It provides tools for full resets, manual and automatic database reinitialization, email and general configuration debugging, and autoinstall processes, all to ensure your Friendica installation remains reliable and easy to maintain."
msgstr "Denne rolle udspiller sig Friendica bruge Docker, styring af Friendica påføringsbeholder ved siden af en central beholder MariaDB Et eksempel. Det giver værktøjer til fuld resets, manuel og automatisk database reinitialisering, e-mail og generel konfiguration debugging, og autoinstallere processer, alle for at sikre din Friendica installation forbliver pålidelig og let at vedligeholde."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "This role deploys Funkwhale using Docker. It orchestrates multiple services (including the API, Frontend, Celery Worker, Celery Beat, and Typesense) integrating with centralized PostgreSQL and Redis services for a fully containerized music sharing experience."
msgstr "Denne rolle udspiller sig Funkwhale Brug Docker. Det organiserer flere tjenester (herunder API, Frontend, Selleri Worker, Selleri Beat, og Typesense) integration med centraliseret PostgreSQL og Redis tjenester til en fuldt containeret musik deling oplevelse."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "This role deploys FusionDirectory on Docker Compose against the project's central `svc-db-openldap` server. The OIDC variant gates the FusionDirectory web UI through `web-app-keycloak`'s SSO-proxy sidecar for SSO; the LDAP variant relies on the same FusionDirectory binding to `svc-db-openldap` as its primary auth path. RBAC follows the LDAP group model that FusionDirectory already understands natively, so no glue layer is required for authorisation mapping."
msgstr "Denne rolle udspiller sig FusionDirectory om Docker Compose mod projektets centrale `svc-db-openldap` server. OIDC-varianten låser FusionDirectory Web UI gennem `web-app-keycloak`SSO- proxy sidevogn til SSO; LDAP-varianten er afhængig af det samme FusionDirectory bindende til `svc-db-openldap` som sin primære auth sti. RBAC følger LDAP gruppe model, der FusionDirectory allerede forstår indbygget, så der er ikke brug for lim lag til godkendelse kortlægning."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "This role deploys FusionDirectory on Docker Compose against the project’s central ``svc-db-openldap`` server. The OIDC variant gates the FusionDirectory web UI through ``web-app-keycloak``\\ ’s SSO-proxy sidecar for SSO; the LDAP variant relies on the same FusionDirectory binding to ``svc-db-openldap`` as its primary auth path. RBAC follows the LDAP group model that FusionDirectory already understands natively, so no glue layer is required for authorisation mapping."
msgstr "Denne rolle udspiller sig FusionDirectory om Docker Compose mod projektets centrale ``svc-db-openldap`` server. OIDC-varianten låser FusionDirectory Web UI gennem ``web-app-keycloak``\\ 's SSO- proxy sidevogn for SSO; LDAP variant bygger på den samme FusionDirectory bindende til ``svc-db-openldap`` som sin primære auth sti. RBAC følger LDAP gruppe model, der FusionDirectory allerede forstår indbygget, så der er ikke brug for lim lag til godkendelse kortlægning."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "This role deploys GitLab from the official Cloud Native GitLab (CNG) CE images at ``registry.gitlab.com/gitlab-org/build/cng/`` as separate services: ``webservice`` (puma), ``sidekiq``, ``workhorse`` (sole HTTP entry point), ``gitaly``, ``shell`` (gitlab-sshd) and a one-shot ``migrations`` job. All images share a single version pin (``services.webservice.version``). PostgreSQL, Redis and S3-compatible object storage are wired through the platform lookups (central or sidecar), OIDC and SMTP through the platform SSO and email services. The front proxy terminates TLS and forwards HTTP to workhorse."
msgstr "Denne rolle udspiller sig GitLab fra den officielle Cloud Native GitLab (CNG) CE-billeder på ``registry.gitlab.com/gitlab-org/build/cng/`` som særskilte tjenester: ``webservice`` (puma), ``sidekiq``, ``workhorse`` (eneste HTTP-indgangspunkt), ``gitaly``, ``shell`` (gitlab- sshd) og et one-shot ``migrations`` job. Alle billeder deler en enkelt version pin (``services.webservice.version``). PostgreSQL Redis og S3-kompatibel objekt opbevaring er kappet gennem platformen opslag (central eller sidevogn), OIDC og SMTP gennem platformen SSO og e-mail-tjenester. Den forreste proxy afslutter TLS og frem HTTP til arbejdshest."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "This role deploys GitLab from the official Cloud Native GitLab (CNG) CE images at `registry.gitlab.com/gitlab-org/build/cng/` as separate services: `webservice` (puma), `sidekiq`, `workhorse` (sole HTTP entry point), `gitaly`, `shell` (gitlab-sshd) and a one-shot `migrations` job. All images share a single version pin (`services.webservice.version`). PostgreSQL, Redis and S3-compatible object storage are wired through the platform lookups (central or sidecar), OIDC and SMTP through the platform SSO and email services. The front proxy terminates TLS and forwards HTTP to workhorse."
msgstr "Denne rolle udspiller sig GitLab fra den officielle Cloud Native GitLab (CNG) CE-billeder på `registry.gitlab.com/gitlab-org/build/cng/` som særskilte tjenester: `webservice` (puma), `sidekiq`, `workhorse` (eneste HTTP-indgangspunkt), `gitaly`, `shell` (gitlab- sshd) og et one-shot `migrations` job. Alle billeder deler en enkelt version pin (`services.webservice.version`). PostgreSQL Redis og S3-kompatibel objekt opbevaring er kappet gennem platformen opslag (central eller sidevogn), OIDC og SMTP gennem platformen SSO og e-mail-tjenester. Den forreste proxy afslutter TLS og frem HTTP til arbejdshest."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "This role deploys Gitea using Docker. It automates the setup and update processes for your self-hosted Git service, integrating with a central MariaDB for the database. With functionalities for updating, recreating the container, variable management, database access, and shell access to the application container, this role streamlines the management of your Gitea instance. With Hermes Agent or OpenClaw deployed alongside it, the role adds a ``gitea-mcp`` sidecar and declares it as the MCP server of the deployment: an internal ``/mcp`` endpoint on the container network plus the Gitea personal access token that MCP clients present."
msgstr "Denne rolle udspiller sig Gitea Brug Docker. Det automatiserer opsætnings- og opdateringsprocesserne for din selvvært Git service, integration med en central MariaDB for databasen. Med funktioner til opdatering, genskabe beholderen, variabel administration, databaseadgang, og shell adgang til applikationsbeholderen, denne rolle strømlines forvaltningen af din Gitea Et eksempel. Med Hermes Agent eller OpenClaw I denne forbindelse er det vigtigt, at ``gitea-mcp`` sidecar og erklærer det som MCP-serveren af indsættelsen: en intern ``/mcp`` Endepunkt på containernettet plus Gitea personlig adgang token, at MCP-klienter til stede."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "This role deploys Gitea using Docker. It automates the setup and update processes for your self-hosted Git service, integrating with a central MariaDB for the database. With functionalities for updating, recreating the container, variable management, database access, and shell access to the application container, this role streamlines the management of your Gitea instance. With Hermes Agent or OpenClaw deployed alongside it, the role adds a `gitea-mcp` sidecar and declares it as the MCP server of the deployment: an internal `/mcp` endpoint on the container network plus the Gitea personal access token that MCP clients present."
msgstr "Denne rolle udspiller sig Gitea Brug Docker. Det automatiserer opsætnings- og opdateringsprocesserne for din selvvært Git service, integration med en central MariaDB for databasen. Med funktioner til opdatering, genskabe beholderen, variabel administration, databaseadgang, og shell adgang til applikationsbeholderen, denne rolle strømlines forvaltningen af din Gitea Et eksempel. Med Hermes Agent eller OpenClaw I denne forbindelse er det vigtigt, at `gitea-mcp` sidecar og erklærer det som MCP-serveren af indsættelsen: en intern `/mcp` Endepunkt på containernettet plus Gitea personlig adgang token, at MCP-klienter til stede."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "This role deploys Hermes Agent in gateway mode as a Docker service, published behind the reverse proxy on its own subdomain, with its compose service pinned to the isolating runtime that the Kata & gVisor role selects for the host. The OpenAI-compatible API answers on the subdomain. The web dashboard is optional and off by default; switched on, it takes the subdomain root and the API stays under `/v1/` and `/health`. The API server is protected by a generated bearer key, and when the LiteLLM Gateway is part of the deployment the agent's model endpoint is pointed at that gateway with a per-consumer virtual key. Agent state lives in a named volume that the Backup Docker Volumes service captures when it is enabled."
msgstr "Denne rolle udspiller sig Hermes Agent i gateway-tilstand som en Docker-tjeneste, der er offentliggjort bag den omvendte proxy på sit eget underdomæne, med sin komponenttjeneste fastgjort til den isolerende runtime, at Kata & gVisor rollevalg for værten. OpenAI- kompatibel API svar på underdomænet. Web dashboard er valgfri og slukket som standard; tændt, det tager subdomæne rod og API ophold under `/v1/` og `/health`. API server er beskyttet af en genereret ihændehavernøgle, og når LiteLLM Gateway er en del af indsættelsen agenten model endpoint er rettet mod denne gateway med en per- forbruger virtuel nøgle. Agent State lever i et navngivet volumen, at Backup Docker Volumes service fanger når den er aktiveret."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "This role deploys Hermes Agent in gateway mode as a Docker service, published behind the reverse proxy on its own subdomain, with its compose service pinned to the isolating runtime that the Kata & gVisor role selects for the host. The OpenAI-compatible API answers on the subdomain. The web dashboard is optional and off by default; switched on, it takes the subdomain root and the API stays under ``/v1/`` and ``/health``. The API server is protected by a generated bearer key, and when the LiteLLM Gateway is part of the deployment the agent’s model endpoint is pointed at that gateway with a per-consumer virtual key. Agent state lives in a named volume that the Backup Docker Volumes service captures when it is enabled."
msgstr "Denne rolle udspiller sig Hermes Agent i gateway-tilstand som en Docker-tjeneste, der er offentliggjort bag den omvendte proxy på sit eget underdomæne, med sin komponenttjeneste fastgjort til den isolerende runtime, at Kata & gVisor rollevalg for værten. OpenAI- kompatibel API svar på underdomænet. Web dashboard er valgfri og slukket som standard; tændt, det tager subdomæne rod og API ophold under ``/v1/`` og ``/health``. API server er beskyttet af en genereret ihændehavernøgle, og når LiteLLM Gateway er en del af indsættelsen agenten model endpoint er rettet mod denne gateway med en per- forbruger virtuel nøgle. Agent State lever i et navngivet volumen, at Backup Docker Volumes service fanger når den er aktiveret."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "This role deploys Home Assistant as a container on its own canonical domain behind the reverse proxy, with the configuration directory kept in a persistent volume. It renders a ``configuration.yaml`` that trusts the proxy through ``use_x_forwarded_for`` and the project-wide trusted-proxy CIDRs, and it attaches the hub to a shared overlay network. With Hermes Agent deployed alongside it, the role declares the hub as the MCP server of the deployment: an internal ``/api/mcp`` endpoint plus the long-lived access token that MCP clients present."
msgstr "Denne rolle udspiller sig Home Assistant som beholder på sit eget kanoniske domæne bag den omvendte proxy, med indstillingsmappen i et vedvarende volumen. Det gør en ``configuration.yaml`` der stoler på proxy gennem ``use_x_forwarded_for`` og projektet-bred trusted- proxy CIDRs, og det binder hub til en delt overlay netværk. Med Hermes Agent indsat ved siden af den, rolle erklærer hub som MCP-serveren af indsættelsen: en intern ``/api/mcp`` Endepunkt plus den langvarige adgang token, som MCP klienter til stede."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "This role deploys Home Assistant as a container on its own canonical domain behind the reverse proxy, with the configuration directory kept in a persistent volume. It renders a `configuration.yaml` that trusts the proxy through `use_x_forwarded_for` and the project-wide trusted-proxy CIDRs, and it attaches the hub to a shared overlay network. With Hermes Agent deployed alongside it, the role declares the hub as the MCP server of the deployment: an internal `/api/mcp` endpoint plus the long-lived access token that MCP clients present."
msgstr "Denne rolle udspiller sig Home Assistant som beholder på sit eget kanoniske domæne bag den omvendte proxy, med indstillingsmappen i et vedvarende volumen. Det gør en `configuration.yaml` der stoler på proxy gennem `use_x_forwarded_for` og projektet-bred trusted- proxy CIDRs, og det binder hub til en delt overlay netværk. Med Hermes Agent indsat ved siden af den, rolle erklærer hub som MCP-serveren af indsættelsen: en intern `/api/mcp` Endepunkt plus den langvarige adgang token, som MCP klienter til stede."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "This role deploys Jenkins on Docker Compose. It builds a custom Jenkins image that pre-installs the ``ldap``, ``role-strategy``, and ``configuration-as-code`` plugins plus every plugin its enabled addons declare, then mounts a JCasC YAML file that wires the security realm against Keycloak (variant 0, OIDC) or ``svc-db-openldap`` (variant 1, LDAP). The setup wizard is skipped via ``JAVA_OPTS=-Djenkins.install.runSetupWizard=false`` so the JCasC config takes over from first boot."
msgstr "Denne rolle udspiller sig Jenkins om Docker ComposeDen bygger en skik Jenkins billede, der præ- installerer ``ldap``, ``role-strategy``, og ``configuration-as-code`` plugins plus hvert plugin dens aktiverede addons erklærer, derefter monterer en JCasC YAML fil, der wirer sikkerhed rige mod Keycloak (variant 0, OIDC) eller ``svc-db-openldap`` (variant 1, LDAP). Opsætningsguiden er sprunget over via ``JAVA_OPTS=-Djenkins.install.runSetupWizard=false`` Så JCasC config overtager fra første støvle."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "This role deploys Jenkins on Docker Compose. It builds a custom Jenkins image that pre-installs the `ldap`, `role-strategy`, and `configuration-as-code` plugins plus every plugin its enabled addons declare, then mounts a JCasC YAML file that wires the security realm against Keycloak (variant 0, OIDC) or `svc-db-openldap` (variant 1, LDAP). The setup wizard is skipped via `JAVA_OPTS=-Djenkins.install.runSetupWizard=false` so the JCasC config takes over from first boot."
msgstr "Denne rolle udspiller sig Jenkins om Docker ComposeDen bygger en skik Jenkins billede, der præ- installerer `ldap`, `role-strategy`, og `configuration-as-code` plugins plus hvert plugin dens aktiverede addons erklærer, derefter monterer en JCasC YAML fil, der wirer sikkerhed rige mod Keycloak (variant 0, OIDC) eller `svc-db-openldap` (variant 1, LDAP). Opsætningsguiden er sprunget over via `JAVA_OPTS=-Djenkins.install.runSetupWizard=false` Så JCasC config overtager fra første støvle."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "This role deploys Joomla on Docker Compose. It builds a custom Joomla image that bakes in Composer for runtime extension builds, runs the Joomla CLI installer with the role's database, and installs the in-role `plg_system_keycloak` plugin so the site speaks OIDC against Keycloak with RBAC group mapping. A matrix-deploy variant flips the role to LDAP via Joomla's core LDAP authentication plugin instead."
msgstr "Denne rolle udspiller sig Joomla om Docker ComposeDen bygger en skik Joomla billede, der bages i Komponist til runtime forlængelse bygger, kører Joomla CLI installering med rollens database, og installerer in- rolle `plg_system_keycloak` plugin så webstedet taler OIDC mod Keycloak med RBAC gruppe mapping. En matrix- deployere variant vender rollen til LDAP via Joomla's centrale LDAP godkendelse plugin i stedet."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "This role deploys Joomla on Docker Compose. It builds a custom Joomla image that bakes in Composer for runtime extension builds, runs the Joomla CLI installer with the role’s database, and installs the in-role ``plg_system_keycloak`` plugin so the site speaks OIDC against Keycloak with RBAC group mapping. A matrix-deploy variant flips the role to LDAP via Joomla’s core LDAP authentication plugin instead."
msgstr "Denne rolle udspiller sig Joomla om Docker ComposeDen bygger en skik Joomla billede, der bages i Komponist til runtime forlængelse bygger, kører Joomla CLI installering med rollens database, og installerer in- rolle ``plg_system_keycloak`` plugin så webstedet taler OIDC mod Keycloak med RBAC gruppe mapping. En matrix- deployere variant vender rollen til LDAP via Joomla's centrale LDAP godkendelse plugin i stedet."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "This role deploys KIX as an Infinito.Nexus web app behind the project's standard `sys-stk-front-proxy` and `web-app-keycloak`'s SSO-proxy sidecar chain. The upstream `kix-on-premise` proxy, backend, and frontend containers ship from `docker-registry.kixdesk.com/public/`. The backend initialises its schema (`scripts/database/kix-schema.xml`) against the central `svc-db-postgres` cluster, or against the embedded postgres sidecar when no central provider is in the inventory, with `pg_trgm` pre-activated via `services.postgres.extensions`; the cache is the role-local passwordless redis sidecar (the frontend ignores `REDIS_CACHE_PASSWORD`). The local `admin` account is seeded via `INITIAL_ADMIN_PW` on first start (see `meta/secrets.yml`) and realigned with the declared credential on every later deploy by `tasks/01_admin.yml`, which runs `files/perl/realign_admin_password.pl` inside the backend."
msgstr "Denne rolle udspiller sig KIX som en Infinito.Nexus webapp bag projektets standard `sys-stk-front-proxy` og `web-app-keycloak`SSO- proxy sidevognskæde. Opstrøms `kix-on-premise` proxy, backend, og frontend containere skib fra `docker-registry.kixdesk.com/public/`. Bagenden initialiserer sit skema (`scripts/database/kix-schema.xml`) mod den centrale `svc-db-postgres` klynge, eller mod den indlejrede postgres sidevogn, når ingen central udbyder er i fortegnelsen, med `pg_trgm` præ- aktiveret via `services.postgres.extensions`; Cachen er den role- lokale passorless rød sidevogn (frontend ignorerer `REDIS_CACHE_PASSWORD`)Den lokale `admin` konto er seedd via `INITIAL_ADMIN_PW` ved første start (Se `meta/secrets.yml`) og justeret med den erklærede kreditværdighed på hver senere deployering af `tasks/01_admin.yml`, der kører `files/perl/realign_admin_password.pl` I bagenden."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "This role deploys KIX as an Infinito.Nexus web app behind the project’s standard ``sys-stk-front-proxy`` and ``web-app-keycloak``\\ ’s SSO-proxy sidecar chain. The upstream ``kix-on-premise`` proxy, backend, and frontend containers ship from ``docker-registry.kixdesk.com/public/``. The backend initialises its schema (``scripts/database/kix-schema.xml``) against the central ``svc-db-postgres`` cluster, or against the embedded postgres sidecar when no central provider is in the inventory, with ``pg_trgm`` pre-activated via ``services.postgres.extensions``; the cache is the role-local passwordless redis sidecar (the frontend ignores ``REDIS_CACHE_PASSWORD``). The local ``admin`` account is seeded via ``INITIAL_ADMIN_PW`` on first start (see ``meta/secrets.yml``) and realigned with the declared credential on every later deploy by ``tasks/01_admin.yml``, which runs ``files/perl/realign_admin_password.pl`` inside the backend."
