msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "This role deploys no AI surface and declares no ``litellm`` service, because EspoCRM’s open-source distribution does not ship one. At the pinned version ``10.0.4``, ``application/Espo/Modules`` contains only ``Crm``, ``application/Espo/Resources/metadata/app/config.json`` declares no AI key, and the release ZIP the image is built from leaves ``custom/Espo/Modules`` empty. The AI features (Summary, Intelligent Paste, AI Email Composer, AI formula functions) live exclusively in the commercial `Intelligence extension <https://www.espocrm.com/extensions/intelligence/>`__, which is closed source, requires a purchased license, and is published in no ``espocrm`` GitHub repository. Bumping the version does not change this: the extension is documented as requiring EspoCRM 10.0.3 or greater, so newer cores stay hosts for it rather than absorbing it."
msgstr "Denne rolle giver ingen AI overflade og erklærer ingen ``litellm`` service, fordi EspoCRMOpen-source distribution ikke sende en. På den fastgjorte version ``10.0.4``, ``application/Espo/Modules`` indeholder kun ``Crm``, ``application/Espo/Resources/metadata/app/config.json`` erklærer ingen AI-nøgle, og udgivelsen ZIP billedet er bygget fra blade ``custom/Espo/Modules`` tom. AI funktioner (Oversigt, Intelligent Paste, AI e-mail-komponist, AI formel funktioner) lever udelukkende i den kommercielle `Intelligence extension <https://www.espocrm.com/extensions/intelligence/>`__, som er lukket kilde, kræver en købt licens, og er offentliggjort i ``espocrm`` GitHub-lageret. Bumping versionen ændrer ikke dette: udvidelsen er dokumenteret som kræver EspoCRM 10.0.3 eller større, så nyere kerner forblive værter for det snarere end at absorbere det."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "This role deploys no AI surface and declares no `litellm` service, because EspoCRM's open-source distribution does not ship one. At the pinned version `10.0.4`, `application/Espo/Modules` contains only `Crm`, `application/Espo/Resources/metadata/app/config.json` declares no AI key, and the release ZIP the image is built from leaves `custom/Espo/Modules` empty. The AI features (Summary, Intelligent Paste, AI Email Composer, AI formula functions) live exclusively in the commercial [Intelligence extension](https://www.espocrm.com/extensions/intelligence/), which is closed source, requires a purchased license, and is published in no `espocrm` GitHub repository. Bumping the version does not change this: the extension is documented as requiring EspoCRM 10.0.3 or greater, so newer cores stay hosts for it rather than absorbing it."
msgstr "Denne rolle giver ingen AI overflade og erklærer ingen `litellm` service, fordi EspoCRMOpen-source distribution ikke sende en. På den fastgjorte version `10.0.4`, `application/Espo/Modules` indeholder kun `Crm`, `application/Espo/Resources/metadata/app/config.json` erklærer ingen AI-nøgle, og udgivelsen ZIP billedet er bygget fra blade `custom/Espo/Modules` tom. AI funktioner (Oversigt, Intelligent Paste, AI e-mail-komponist, AI formel funktioner) lever udelukkende i den kommercielle [Efterretningsudvidelse](https://www.espocrm.com/extensions/intelligence/), som er lukket kilde, kræver en købt licens, og er offentliggjort i `espocrm` GitHub-lageret. Bumping versionen ændrer ikke dette: udvidelsen er dokumenteret som kræver EspoCRM 10.0.3 eller større, så nyere kerner forblive værter for det snarere end at absorbere det."

msgid "This role deploys no third-party application, so the licence above is the only one that applies."
msgstr ""

msgid "This role deploys nothing. Its ``meta/services.yml`` pins the image and release each distribution’s development environment boots from, keyed by the distribution id of `meta/distros.yml <../../meta/distros.yml>`__, and ``utils/distros.py`` reads the workspace matrix from it. Because the pins live in a role’s ``meta/services.yml``, the docker updater proposes new releases as pull requests and the image mirror and the vulnerability scan cover them like every other role image. ``follow: latest`` holds a pin to the release the ``latest`` tag points at, so Ubuntu moves between LTS releases only and Fedora skips rawhide. Arch stays rolling, and CentOS Stream tags carry no number the updater can order, so its next stream is a manual change."
msgstr ""

msgid "This role deploys nothing. Its `meta/services.yml` pins the image and release each distribution's development environment boots from, keyed by the distribution id of [meta/distros.yml](../../meta/distros.yml), and `utils/distros.py` reads the workspace matrix from it. Because the pins live in a role's `meta/services.yml`, the docker updater proposes new releases as pull requests and the image mirror and the vulnerability scan cover them like every other role image. `follow: latest` holds a pin to the release the `latest` tag points at, so Ubuntu moves between LTS releases only and Fedora skips rawhide. Arch stays rolling, and CentOS Stream tags carry no number the updater can order, so its next stream is a manual change."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "This role deploys the LiteLLM admin UI as the browser-facing entry point of the headless LiteLLM Gateway. It runs in host mode and starts no container of its own: it claims a canonical domain, terminates TLS, applies the platform Content-Security-Policy, and reverse-proxies that domain to the local HTTP port the gateway publishes. Visitors sign in with the gateway's own UI credentials."
msgstr "Denne rolle udnytter LiteLLM admin UI som browseren-vender indgang til hovedløse LiteLLM Gateway. Det kører i værtstilstand og starter ingen beholder af sin egen: det kræver et kanonisk domæne, afslutter TLS, anvender platformen Content- Security- Policy, og reverse- proxy dette domæne til den lokale HTTP port gateway publicerer. Besøgende melder sig hos gateways egne UI-papirer."

