msgid "Walks the same edges the constructor's role set is built from, so a whitelist-scoped deploy and the full-inventory deploy agree on what a role depends on. The traversal itself lives in ``utils/roles/applications/in_group_deps``; this only exposes it to Ansible."
msgstr "Går de samme kanter konstruktørens rolle sæt er bygget fra, så en whitelist- scoped deployering og full-inventory deployering enige om, hvad en rolle afhænger af. Traversen selv bor i ``utils/roles/applications/in_group_deps``; dette kun udsætter det for Ansible."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Walks up from ``start`` (default: current working directory) until a ``.env`` is found; returns ``None`` if none exists in any parent."
msgstr "Går op fra ``start`` (standard: nuværende arbejdsmappe) til ``.env`` er fundet; vender tilbage ``None`` hvis ingen findes i nogen forælder."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Walks up to ``limit`` recent runs because the very latest run on a branch is often a lint-only or skipped event with no deploy matrix."
msgstr "Går op til ``limit`` seneste kører, fordi den allernyeste køre på en gren er ofte en lint- kun eller sprunget begivenhed uden implementering matrix."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Wall content is baked at deploy time from ``services.fediwall.walls``, so administration happens in Ansible rather than in an in-app admin panel. The persona-facing coverage this role does carry lives in the cross-fediverse scenarios that post on a Mastodon or Friendica sibling and assert the post appears on the wall."
msgstr "Vægindhold bages på deployeringstid fra ``services.fediwall.walls``, så administration sker i Ansible snarere end i en in-app admin panel. Den person-står over for dækning denne rolle bærer liv i cross-fevarious scenarier, der sender på en Mastodon eller Friendica Siblende og hævde posten vises på væggen."

