# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "With `seaweedfs` disabled Active Storage uses the local Disk service and writes below `/code/storage`, which is on no volume: `meta/volumes.yml` mounts `/app/public/uploads` and `/app/log`, and the app at `/code` writes to neither (both empty on the compose stack). Measured on that stack: `ActiveStorage::Blob.service.name` is `local`, and after a role sync had recreated the container `/code/storage` held 5 files for 740 blob records, so every seeded image, avatar and attachment answered as a broken image. `files/ruby/ensure/design.rb` attaches its own logo and favicon again when their files are gone. Options: mount a volume at `/code/storage`, or point the two existing volumes at the paths the app uses."
