msgid "[ ] translator: after `agents.translator.max_attempts` failed attempts an entry is no longer retried, stays marked for a human, and is listed in the translator's report (fixture of a string every engine fails)."
msgstr ""

msgid "[ ] translator: an algorithm pull request carries the benchmark table per language, and a change that lowers any language's score is discarded (fixture)."
msgstr ""

msgid "[ ] translator: an entry that fails the separate `make test-oracle` judgement is retranslated in the next window with the engine that produced it excluded."
msgstr ""

msgid "[ ] translator: at 23:00 UTC the night cron starts or resumes translation regardless of load, and at 07:00 UTC it pauses it and hands over to the day rule (fixture clock). Partly met: `agents/roles/translator/cron.yml` carries the start and pause entries of both windows and `utils/orchestrator/load.py` lets a pause outrank a start of the same tick (`tests/unit/python/utils/orchestrator/test_load.py`); the orchestrator scheduler does not pass measured conditions to `cron.due` and does not act on the result yet."
msgstr ""

#, no-python-format
msgid "[ ] translator: during the day, a tick with CPU and GPU below 30 % starts or resumes translation, and a tick with CPU or GPU above 95 % pauses it (fixture load figures). Partly met: as above, `conditions` in `utils/orchestrator/load.py`; the load sampling in the orchestrator is missing."
msgstr ""

msgid "[ ] translator: each language gets its own pull request with only that language's catalogs, and no language pull request contains algorithm changes."
msgstr ""

msgid "[ ] translator: new strings get machine translations through `web-svc-translate` as Weblate suggestions, and a human-reviewed string stays unchanged."
msgstr ""

msgid "[ ] translator: on a host where `accelerated()` is false, the GPU condition counts as met. Partly met: `conditions(..., accelerated=False)` in `utils/orchestrator/load.py`; the orchestrator does not read `accelerated()` yet."
msgstr ""

msgid "[ ] translator: the day rule ignores the translation lane's own load, so a running translation at high own load with an idle rest of the system is not paused (fixture). Partly met: `rest_of_system` in `utils/orchestrator/load.py` with its red fixture; the per-container lane sample is missing."
msgstr ""

msgid "[ ] translator: the evaluation set of each language is built from human-reviewed Weblate strings and is not used as translation input."
msgstr ""

msgid "[ ] translator: the judge pass of a full night stays within its budget of about one hour of the window, measured on the host (recorded duration)."
msgstr ""

msgid "[ ] translator: the language set equals `domain_languages()` for each domain, only languages with changed catalogs get a pull request, and a language without a docs catalog gets it created in its first pull request."
msgstr ""

msgid "[ ] vCPU, RAM and disk of a running agent VM, read back from the hypervisor, equal its `workspace.resources`. `[ci]`"
msgstr ""

msgid "[ ] web-app-postmarks: Postmarks reads `site_name` only from `account.json`, which switches on fediverse mode, so the image build patches `server.js` to read `SITE_NAME`, rendered from the design title, into the page title, the header and both Atom feed titles (upstream option in `roles/web-app-postmarks/TODO.md`). Open: one green run of the complete spec on this state, with a design title that differs from `Postmarks`."
msgstr ""

msgid "[ ] web-app-stalwart: under `sso` the web administration specs need its administrator group grant (`199f2a6d41`), which `feature/designer` does not carry and `feature/store-i18n` and `feature/iam-profile-rbac` do. Open: one green run of the complete stalwart spec with `design`, `sso` and `email` (variant 0) on the merged state of either line."
msgstr ""

msgid "[ ] web-app-wazuh contains no network-specific code (no onion variable, no second front-proxy include, no forked vhost template) and passes a `multi` row including the onion leak pass."
msgstr ""

