# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[x] When a service runs with `DEPLOYMENT_MODE: swarm`, ALL its volumes MUST opt into NFS AND `storage.backend: nfs`; otherwise the service's role group should not contain multiple hosts. Mixing local-only volumes into a multi-host role is a configuration error unless each local-only volume carries `nfs: false` AND every service mounting it carries a per-service `placement`, so the task cannot be scheduled away from the node holding the data. The placement-constraint fallback used in earlier drafts is dropped in favour of free task placement (option 2b from the design brainstorm)."
msgstr "[x] Når en tjeneste kører med `DEPLOYMENT_MODE: swarm`, alle dens mængder skal vælge i NFS og `storage.backend: nfs`; ellers bør tjenestens rollegruppe ikke indeholde flere værter. Blanding local- only volumener i en multi- host rolle er en konfiguration fejl, medmindre hver local- only volumen bærer `nfs: false` Og hver service montering det bærer en per- service `placement`, så opgaven kan ikke planlægges væk fra node holder data. Den pladsbegrænsning, der anvendes i tidligere udkast, er faldet til fordel for gratis opgaveplacering. (option 2b fra design brainstorm)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[x] When a service runs with `DEPLOYMENT_MODE: swarm`, every per-role network declared today as `driver: bridge` MUST be rendered as `driver: overlay` with `attachable: true`. Cross-node service-to-service traffic depends on this — `bridge` networks are node-local and would break the swarm mesh."
msgstr "[x] Når en tjeneste kører med `DEPLOYMENT_MODE: swarm`, hvert perrollenetværk erklærede i dag som `driver: bridge` SKAL afleveres som `driver: overlay` med `attachable: true`. Cross-node service-to-service trafik afhænger af dette - `bridge` netværk er node- lokale og ville bryde sværm mesh."

