msgid "``mcp.credential.owner`` names the principal in the users dict, which is the key the token store writes under. ``basic_auth`` is the one scheme that puts a name on the wire, and the name it needs is the principal's ``username``: the two differ as soon as the account shortens its name, and presenting the key then authenticates nobody. Bearer schemes present no user name at all, so for them this answer is a label the renderer never sends."
