# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`gh api` switches implicitly from GET to POST as soon as a body-flag is present; no explicit `-X`/`--method` is required. Without these ask rules the broad `Bash(*)` allow would let body-carrying `gh api` POSTs through silently. Short forms (`-f`, `-F`), long forms (`--field`, `--raw-field`), and file input (`--input`) are all listed so no spelling slips past. A future gh-CLI body-flag would need to be added here explicitly."
msgstr "`gh api` skifter implicit fra GET til POST så snart et body- flag er til stede; ingen eksplicit `-X`/`--method` er påkrævet. Uden disse spørger regler den brede `Bash(*)` tillade ville lade body- carriage `gh api` POST 'er gennem lydløst. Korte former (`-f`, `-F`), lange former (`--field`, `--raw-field`), og fil input (`--input`) er alle anført, så ingen stavefejl forbi. Et fremtidigt gh- CLI body- flag skal tilføjes her eksplicit."

# der kører næste gang nogen `gh` subcommand åbner en editor (F.eks. `gh issue
# create` uden `--body`), en deferred- henrettelse bagdør, der overlever den
# nuværende session. Vedvarende CLI config tilhører en bevidst
# operatørbeslutning.
# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`gh config set editor /tmp/evil.sh` plants a binary that runs the next time any `gh` subcommand opens an editor (e.g. `gh issue create` without `--body`), a deferred-execution backdoor that survives the current session. Persistent CLI config belongs to a deliberate operator decision."
msgstr "`gh config set editor /tmp/evil.sh` planter en binær, der kører næste gang nogen `gh` subcommand åbner en editor (F.eks. `gh issue create` uden `--body`), en deferred- henrettelse bagdør, der overlever den nuværende session. Vedvarende CLI config tilhører en bevidst operatørbeslutning."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`gh` CLI's cache directory (HTTP response cache + extension metadata). Granted because every `gh` invocation writes cache entries at startup; denying it would require every `gh` call to be wrapped with an `XDG_CACHE_HOME=/tmp/...` env prefix, which adds a shell shape that falls out of sandbox auto-allow and forces per-subcommand allow entries. Auth tokens are **not** stored here (they live in `~/.config/gh/`, which stays read-only). Persistence trade-off is identical to `~/.cache/pip` / `~/.cache/pre-commit`: cache poisoning, if it occurred, would survive reboots, but API auth is server-side so the blast radius is bounded to wrong-output-to-operator."
msgstr "`gh` CLI 's cache mappe (HTTP- svarcache + udvidelsesmetadata). Det er givet, fordi alle `gh` invocation skriver cache poster ved opstart; benægtelse af det ville kræve hver `gh` opfordring til at blive pakket ind med en `XDG_CACHE_HOME=/tmp/...` env prefix, som tilføjer en shell form, der falder ud af sandkasse auto- tillad og styrker per-underkommando tillader poster. Auth tokens er **ikke** opbevares her (De bor i `~/.config/gh/`, som kun holder sig af-)Persistence tradeoff er identisk med `~/.cache/pip` / `~/.cache/pre-commit`: cache forgiftning, hvis det skete, ville overleve genstøvler, men API Auth er serverside, så sprængradius er begrænset til uretmæssig-output- to- operatør."

