msgid "`sso` gates `STALWART_SSO_ENABLED` together with `services.sso.enabled`, so it decides whether the authentication singleton points at the Keycloak OIDC directory (`tasks/06_oidc.yml`) and whether Roundcube logs in over OAuth (`templates/roundcube-oauth.inc.php.j2`). Turning it off on a server that already uses the OIDC directory does not point the singleton back at the Internal directory."
msgstr ""

msgid "`sso` renders the `OPENID_CONNECT_*` block of [templates/env.j2](./templates/env.j2). With it Greenlight v3 shows one Sign In button that posts to Keycloak and no Sign Up, and its API refuses every local sign-in except a SuperAdmin's and every local sign-up. Greenlight finds the account by `external_id`, the token's `sub` (`OPENID_CONNECT_UID_FIELD=sub`), and never by e-mail (`USE_EMAIL_AS_EXTERNAL_ID_FALLBACK=false`); [files/ruby/greenlight/ensure_admin.rb](./files/ruby/greenlight/ensure_admin.rb) gives the administrator the Keycloak id that [roles/web-app-keycloak/tasks/utils/directory_users.yml](../web-app-keycloak/tasks/utils/directory_users.yml) reads at deploy."
msgstr ""

msgid "`sso` renders the `WEBLATE_SOCIAL_AUTH_OIDC_*` backend; `WEBLATE_REGISTRATION_ALLOW_BACKENDS=oidc` lets a Keycloak sign-in create its account while local registration is closed. A sign-in reaches an existing account only through its `oidc` link keyed by the token's `sub`, never by e-mail: [files/python/settings_override.py](./files/python/settings_override.py), mounted at `/app/data/settings-override.py`, drops `associate_by_email` from the pipeline, and [files/python/adopt_admin.py](./files/python/adopt_admin.py) links the administrator to the Keycloak id that [roles/web-app-keycloak/tasks/utils/directory_users.yml](../web-app-keycloak/tasks/utils/directory_users.yml) reads at deploy."
msgstr ""

msgid "`sso`: the Keycloak OAuth source (`tasks/setup/oidc.yml`, removed by `tasks/cleanup/oidc.yml` when off). With it on, `[oauth2_client] ENABLE_AUTO_REGISTRATION=true` creates the Gitea account at the first sign-in and `ACCOUNT_LINKING=auto` links a Keycloak identity to the existing account of the same username, so directory accounts synced by the LDAP source and the platform administrator sign in through Keycloak without a link page."
msgstr ""

msgid "`sso`: the Keycloak entry of `oidc_providers` (`templates/flavor/compose/synapse/homeserver.yaml.j2`, `matrix_synapse_oidc_*` in `templates/flavor/ansible/vars.yml.j2`)."
msgstr ""

msgid "`sso`: the `OAUTH_*` and `OPENID_*` block of the Keycloak client."
msgstr ""

msgid "`sso`: the `enabled` flag of the Keycloak `auth.oauth.provider` row (\"Login with SSO\")."
msgstr ""

msgid "`sso`: the `openid_connect` OmniAuth provider in `templates/config/gitlab.yml.j2`."
msgstr ""

msgid "`stalwart-migrate` 1.0.0 to 1.0.3 report differences where none exist: email `keywords` holding a `\\` system flag, contact card `vcard` with extra vCard 3.0 `N` or `ADR` components, and certificate or IP ban settings that the 1.x start inside the tool refreshes or expires. These releases also skip accounts that have no change counter. When the rows are only of these kinds and the state was written by such a release, start over with the pinned release: as a PostgreSQL superuser run `DROP DATABASE stalwart_v1;`, move `migrate-v016/state` aside and deploy again."
msgstr ""

msgid "`start.yml <tasks/utils/prepull/start.yml>`__ pulls the images the deploy of the host runs, as listed by the ``update_pull_images`` filter, that the host does not hold yet under the pinned reference (`pull.yml <tasks/utils/prepull/pull.yml>`__), three at a time in a background job right before the shared services load; with nothing missing no job starts. It runs when ``STORAGE_CONSTRAINED`` and ``RESET`` are false and the host is a stack host, so never on a swarm worker. `reap.yml <tasks/utils/prepull/reap.yml>`__ collects the job before the E2E run, or at the start of the destructor on a host without a server stage, and prints the pulls that failed. A failed pull or the time limit of ``SYS_SVC_CONTAINER_PREPULL_ASYNC_TIME`` does not fail the deploy, and each app still pulls its images itself."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`start_interval` is the cadence while `start_period` is still running. Without it a probe only fires every `interval`, so a service ready after three seconds is reported healthy at the next tick -- 30s, or a minute for the curl flavors -- and a stack converges no faster than its slowest quantisation. It changes when the same probe runs, never what it tests."
msgstr "`start_interval` er kadence mens `start_period` er stadig kører. Uden den skyder en sonde kun alle. `interval`, så en service klar efter tre sekunder er rapporteret sund ved næste kryds -- 30s, eller et minut for krøller varianter -- og en stak konvergerer ikke hurtigere end sin langsommere kvantisering. Det ændrer sig, når den samme sonde løber, aldrig hvad den tester."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`start_period` therefore bounds it: once the window closes the cadence falls back to `interval`, so a service that becomes ready just after the window pays a full tick anyway. The window has to outlast a realistic boot, not merely a fast one, which is why it is measured in minutes rather than sized to `interval`. It costs nothing while the container works, only the time until a broken one is called unhealthy."
msgstr "`start_period` Derfor grænser det: Når vinduet lukker kadence falder tilbage til `interval`, så en tjeneste, der bliver klar lige efter vinduet betaler en fuld tick alligevel. Vinduet skal holde en realistisk støvle, ikke blot en hurtig, hvilket er grunden til, at det måles i minutter i stedet for størrelse til `interval`Det koster intet, mens containeren virker, kun tiden indtil en knækket en kaldes usund."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`stdio_only`, not `hosted_only`. The audit of `discourse/discourse-mcp` at `v0.3.1` closed the sidecar path: ownership, licence, pinning and read-only default pass, but the HTTP transport serves one session per process. Nothing is enabled until upstream supports concurrent sessions."
msgstr "`stdio_only`, ikke `hosted_only`. Revision af `discourse/discourse-mcp` på `v0.3.1` lukkede sidecar stien: ejerskab, licens, pinning og read- only standard pass, men HTTP transport tjener en session per proces. Intet er aktiveret indtil opstrøms understøtter samtidige sessioner."

